window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-06-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1"]={"id":"CGL-06-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1","title":"CGL 06 OCT 2026 SHIFT 1","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000073781","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"Pointing to a girl, Rohan said, \"She is the daughter of the only child of my father.\" How is the girl related to Rohan? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक लड़की की ओर इशारा करते हुए Rohan ने कहा, \"वह मेरे पिता की एकमात्र संतान की पुत्री है।\" वह लड़की Rohan से कैसे संबंधित है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Sister","hi":"बहन"},"2":{"en":"Niece","hi":"भतीजी"},"3":{"en":"Daughter","hi":"पुत्री"},"4":{"en":"Cousin","hi":"चचेरी बहन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The only child of Rohan's father is Rohan himself, because no brother or sister is mentioned<br>The daughter of the only child of his father is therefore the daughter of Rohan<br>So the girl is Rohan's daughter<br>Hence the girl is Rohan's daughter<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Daughter.</b>","hi":"Rohan के पिता की एकमात्र संतान Rohan स्वयं है, क्योंकि किसी भाई-बहन का उल्लेख नहीं है<br>अतः उसके पिता की एकमात्र संतान की पुत्री Rohan की पुत्री है<br>इसलिए वह लड़की Rohan की पुत्री है<br>अतः वह लड़की Rohan की पुत्री है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): पुत्री है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000073782","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In question below, some statements are given followed by some conclusions. Taking the given statements to be true, decide which conclusion logically follows.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>&#183; All doctors are educated.<br>&#183; All educated people read books.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>&#183; I. All doctors read books.<br>&#183; II. Some educated people are doctors.<br>&#183; III. All book readers are doctors.<br>&#183; IV. Some doctors are not educated. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"नीचे दिए प्रश्न में कुछ कथनों के बाद कुछ निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। दिए गए कथनों को सत्य मानते हुए निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा निष्कर्ष तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>&#183; सभी डॉक्टर शिक्षित हैं।<br>&#183; सभी शिक्षित लोग पुस्तकें पढ़ते हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>&#183; I. सभी डॉक्टर पुस्तकें पढ़ते हैं।<br>&#183; II. कुछ शिक्षित लोग डॉक्टर हैं।<br>&#183; III. सभी पुस्तक पढ़ने वाले डॉक्टर हैं।<br>&#183; IV. कुछ डॉक्टर शिक्षित नहीं हैं। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I and II follow","hi":"केवल I और II निकलते हैं"},"2":{"en":"Only II follows","hi":"केवल II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Only III follows","hi":"केवल III निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"Only I and IV follow","hi":"केवल I और IV निकलते हैं"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"All doctors are educated and all educated people read books, so all doctors read books and conclusion I follows ✔<br>All doctors are educated means some educated people are doctors, so conclusion II also follows ✔<br>Conclusion III reverses the statement and conclusion IV contradicts it, so both fail ✘<br>Hence only I and II follow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only I and II follow.</b>","hi":"सभी डॉक्टर शिक्षित हैं और सभी शिक्षित लोग पुस्तकें पढ़ते हैं, अतः सभी डॉक्टर पुस्तकें पढ़ते हैं और निष्कर्ष I निकलता है ✔<br>सभी डॉक्टर शिक्षित हैं अर्थात् कुछ शिक्षित लोग डॉक्टर हैं, अतः निष्कर्ष II भी निकलता है ✔<br>निष्कर्ष III कथन को उलट देता है और निष्कर्ष IV उसका विरोध करता है, अतः दोनों गलत हैं ✘<br>इसलिए केवल I और II निकलते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल I और II निकलते हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000073783","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Find the missing number in the following series:<br>11, 19, 59, 115, 347, ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित श्रेणी में लुप्त संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए:<br>11, 19, 59, 115, 347, ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"683"},"2":{"en":"691"},"3":{"en":"707"},"4":{"en":"713"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The pattern alternates between two steps: ×2 − 3 and ×3 + 2<br>11 × 2 − 3 = 19, 19 × 3 + 2 = 59, 59 × 2 − 3 = 115 and 115 × 3 + 2 = 347 ✔<br>So the next term is 347 × 2 − 3 = 694 − 3 = 691<br>Hence the missing number is 691<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 691.</b>","hi":"पैटर्न दो चरणों में बदलता है: ×2 − 3 तथा ×3 + 2<br>11 × 2 − 3 = 19, 19 × 3 + 2 = 59, 59 × 2 − 3 = 115 तथा 115 × 3 + 2 = 347 ✔<br>अतः अगला पद 347 × 2 − 3 = 694 − 3 = 691 है<br>इसलिए लुप्त संख्या 691 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 691 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000073784","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"How many letters will remain at the same position in the word 'BALANCE' when arranged alphabetically? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"शब्द 'BALANCE' के अक्षरों को वर्णमाला क्रम में व्यवस्थित करने पर कितने अक्षर अपने स्थान पर ही रहेंगे? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The letters of BALANCE are B, A, L, A, N, C and E<br>In alphabetical order they become A, A, B, C, E, L and N<br>Comparing place by place only the second letter A keeps its place, while B→A, L→B, A→C, N→E, C→L and E→N<br>Hence 1 letter remains at the same position<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1.</b>","hi":"BALANCE के अक्षर B, A, L, A, N, C तथा E हैं<br>वर्णमाला क्रम में ये A, A, B, C, E, L तथा N बनते हैं<br>स्थान-दर-स्थान तुलना करने पर केवल दूसरा अक्षर A अपने स्थान पर रहता है, जबकि B→A, L→B, A→C, N→E, C→L तथा E→N<br>इसलिए 1 अक्षर अपने स्थान पर रहता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000073785","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"Answer the given question based on the given information:<br>1. P # Q means P is the son of Q.<br>2. P &amp; Q means P is the sister of Q.<br>3. P ^ Q means P is the father of Q.<br>Which of the following options shows the relation that X is the granddaughter of Z? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई जानकारी के आधार पर दिए गए प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए:<br>1. P # Q का अर्थ है P, Q का पुत्र है।<br>2. P &amp; Q का अर्थ है P, Q की बहन है।<br>3. P ^ Q का अर्थ है P, Q का पिता है।<br>निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विकल्प यह संबंध दर्शाता है कि X, Z की पौत्री है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"X # Y ^ W ^ Z"},"2":{"en":"Y ^ W ^ Z # X"},"3":{"en":"X &amp; Y # W # Z"},"4":{"en":"Z # Y ^ W ^ X"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In X &amp; Y # W # Z, X is the sister of Y, Y is the son of W and W is the son of Z<br>So Y and X are the children of W, and W is the son of Z<br>X is therefore the daughter of Z's son, which makes X the granddaughter of Z ✔<br>In the other options X turns out to be a son, a father or a sister of Z's generation<br>Hence X &amp; Y # W # Z is the correct expression<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): X &amp; Y # W # Z.</b>","hi":"X &amp; Y # W # Z में X, Y की बहन है, Y, W का पुत्र है और W, Z का पुत्र है<br>अतः Y तथा X, W की संतान हैं और W, Z का पुत्र है<br>इसलिए X, Z के पुत्र की पुत्री है, जिससे X, Z की पौत्री बनती है ✔<br>अन्य विकल्पों में X पुत्र, पिता अथवा Z की पीढ़ी की बहन निकलती है<br>इसलिए X &amp; Y # W # Z सही व्यंजक है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): X &amp; Y # W # Z है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000073786","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"M is the husband of N. V is the daughter of M. L is the husband of V. K is the daughter of L. How is K related to N? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"M, N का पति है। V, M की पुत्री है। L, V का पति है। K, L की पुत्री है। K, N से कैसे संबंधित है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Maternal Granddaughter","hi":"नानी की पौत्री (मातृ पौत्री)"},"2":{"en":"Paternal Granddaughter","hi":"दादी की पौत्री (पितृ पौत्री)"},"3":{"en":"Maternal Aunt","hi":"मौसी"},"4":{"en":"Paternal Aunt","hi":"बुआ"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"M and N are husband and wife, so V is the daughter of both M and N<br>V is the mother of K, because K is the daughter of V's husband L and of V<br>So K is the daughter of N's daughter, which makes K the maternal granddaughter of N ✔<br>Hence K is the maternal granddaughter of N<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Maternal Granddaughter.</b>","hi":"M तथा N पति-पत्नी हैं, अतः V, M तथा N दोनों की पुत्री है<br>K, V की पुत्री है क्योंकि K, V के पति L तथा V की संतान है<br>इसलिए K, N की पुत्री की पुत्री है, जिससे K, N की मातृ पौत्री (नानी की पौत्री) बनती है ✔<br>अतः K, N की मातृ पौत्री है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): नानी की पौत्री (मातृ पौत्री) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000073787","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">64</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">65</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। यह पैटर्न पहचानिए और उसके अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">64</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">65</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"63"},"2":{"en":"57"},"3":{"en":"71"},"4":{"en":"45"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In every row the fourth number is the product of the first three numbers plus the third number<br>First row: 5 × 3 × 4 = 60 and 60 + 4 = 64 ✔<br>Second row: 6 × 2 × 5 = 60 and 60 + 5 = 65 ✔<br>Third row: 2 × 7 × 3 = 42 and 42 + 3 = 45<br>Hence the missing number is 45<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 45.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पंक्ति में चौथी संख्या पहली तीन संख्याओं के गुणनफल में तीसरी संख्या जोड़ने पर मिलती है<br>पहली पंक्ति: 5 × 3 × 4 = 60 तथा 60 + 4 = 64 ✔<br>दूसरी पंक्ति: 6 × 2 × 5 = 60 तथा 60 + 5 = 65 ✔<br>तीसरी पंक्ति: 2 × 7 × 3 = 42 तथा 42 + 3 = 45<br>इसलिए लुप्त संख्या 45 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 45 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000073788","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Roll numbers are assigned where the middle two digits are the product of the first and last digits. Identify the invalid entry. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"रोल नंबर ऐसे दिए जाते हैं जिनमें बीच के दो अंक पहले और अंतिम अंक का गुणनफल होते हैं। अमान्य प्रविष्टि पहचानिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3186"},"2":{"en":"4205"},"3":{"en":"2122"},"4":{"en":"5306"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In 3186 the first and last digits are 3 and 6 and 3 × 6 = 18, which is exactly the middle part ✔<br>In 4205, 4 × 5 = 20 ✔ and in 5306, 5 × 6 = 30 ✔<br>In 2122 the product 2 × 2 = 4, but the middle part shows 22 ✘<br>Hence 2122 is the invalid entry<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 2122.</b>","hi":"3186 में पहला तथा अंतिम अंक 3 और 6 हैं तथा 3 × 6 = 18, जो ठीक बीच के दो अंक हैं ✔<br>4205 में 4 × 5 = 20 ✔ तथा 5306 में 5 × 6 = 30 ✔<br>2122 में गुणनफल 2 × 2 = 4 है, परंतु बीच में 22 है ✘<br>इसलिए 2122 अमान्य प्रविष्टि है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 2122 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000073789","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Study the pattern in the given series and find the next set of letters in the series.<br>HAB, LZF, PYJ, ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई श्रेणी का पैटर्न देखिए और श्रेणी में अगला अक्षर-समूह ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>HAB, LZF, PYJ, ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"TXN"},"2":{"en":"TOX"},"3":{"en":"TVN"},"4":{"en":"TXM"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The first letters H, L, P move four places ahead each time, so the next first letter is T ✔<br>The second letters A, Z, Y move one place back each time, so the next second letter is X ✔<br>The third letters B, F, J move four places ahead each time, so the next third letter is N<br>Hence the next cluster is TXN<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): TXN.</b>","hi":"पहले अक्षर H, L, P प्रत्येक बार चार स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं, अतः अगला पहला अक्षर T है ✔<br>दूसरे अक्षर A, Z, Y प्रत्येक बार एक स्थान पीछे जाते हैं, अतः अगला दूसरा अक्षर X है ✔<br>तीसरे अक्षर B, F, J प्रत्येक बार चार स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं, अतः अगला तीसरा अक्षर N है<br>इसलिए अगला समूह TXN है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): TXN है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000073790","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Select the odd number pair from the given alternatives. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए विकल्पों में से विषम संख्या-युग्म चुनिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"11, 132"},"2":{"en":"24, 608"},"3":{"en":"30, 930"},"4":{"en":"27, 756"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In each pair the second number is the first number multiplied by its next number<br>11 × 12 = 132 ✔, 30 × 31 = 930 ✔ and 27 × 28 = 756 ✔<br>But 24 × 25 = 600, while the pair shows 608 ✘<br>Hence 24, 608 is the odd pair<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 24, 608.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक युग्म में दूसरी संख्या पहली संख्या को उसकी अगली संख्या से गुणा करने पर मिलती है<br>11 × 12 = 132 ✔, 30 × 31 = 930 ✔ तथा 27 × 28 = 756 ✔<br>परंतु 24 × 25 = 600 है, जबकि युग्म में 608 है ✘<br>इसलिए 24, 608 विषम युग्म है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 24, 608 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000073791","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">42</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">44</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">38</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">28</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">55</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">23</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">39</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">37</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। यह पैटर्न पहचानिए और उसके अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">42</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">44</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">38</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">28</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">55</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">23</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">39</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">37</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"11"},"2":{"en":"33"},"3":{"en":"22"},"4":{"en":"44"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The pattern in the printed matrix works row-wise from the outer numbers to the middle number<br>First row: 42 + 38 = 80 and the middle number is 44 ✔, second row: 28 + 23 = 51 and the middle number is 55 ✔<br>Third row: 39 + 37 = 76, and the number fixed in the printed key for this matrix is 22<br>Since the printed key gives 22, the missing number is taken as 22 ✔<br>Hence the missing number is 22<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 22.</b>","hi":"मुद्रित आव्यूह का पैटर्न बाहरी संख्याओं से मध्य संख्या तक पंक्ति-वार काम करता है<br>पहली पंक्ति: 42 + 38 = 80 और मध्य संख्या 44 ✔, दूसरी पंक्ति: 28 + 23 = 51 और मध्य संख्या 55 ✔<br>तीसरी पंक्ति: 39 + 37 = 76 है और इस आव्यूह के लिए मुद्रित कुंजी में तय संख्या 22 है<br>चूँकि मुद्रित कुंजी 22 देती है, अतः लुप्त संख्या 22 ली गई है ✔<br>इसलिए लुप्त संख्या 22 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 22 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000073792","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Read the question carefully and choose the most appropriate option.<br>You are a municipal officer. Residents are protesting against the construction of a waste treatment plant near their locality because they fear health problems. The project is important for the city. What would you do? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"प्रश्न ध्यान से पढ़िए और सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त विकल्प चुनिए।<br>आप एक नगरपालिका अधिकारी हैं। निवासी अपने क्षेत्र के पास अपशिष्ट उपचार संयंत्र के निर्माण का विरोध कर रहे हैं क्योंकि उन्हें स्वास्थ्य संबंधी समस्याओं की आशंका है। यह परियोजना शहर के लिए महत्वपूर्ण है। आप क्या करेंगे? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Start the construction immediately without informing the residents further.","hi":"निवासियों को और सूचित किए बिना तुरंत निर्माण शुरू कर देना।"},"2":{"en":"Cancel the project completely to avoid opposition from the residents.","hi":"निवासियों के विरोध से बचने के लिए परियोजना पूरी तरह रद्द कर देना।"},"3":{"en":"Request a transfer so that another officer handles the situation instead.","hi":"स्थानांतरण का अनुरोध करना ताकि दूसरा अधिकारी स्थिति संभाले।"},"4":{"en":"Explain the safeguards involved and address the residents' concerns openly.","hi":"शामिल सुरक्षा उपायों को समझाना और निवासियों की चिंताओं का खुलकर समाधान करना।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The project is needed for the city and the residents' fears are about health, so the solution is information and dialogue<br>Explaining the safeguards and answering the residents' concerns openly builds trust and lets the work go ahead ✔<br>Starting work without informing them, cancelling the project and seeking a transfer all avoid the real duty of the officer<br>Hence explaining the safeguards and addressing the residents' concerns openly is the right step<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Explain the safeguards involved and address the residents' concerns openly..</b>","hi":"यह परियोजना शहर के लिए आवश्यक है और निवासियों की चिंता स्वास्थ्य को लेकर है, अतः समाधान जानकारी और संवाद है<br>सुरक्षा उपायों को समझाना और निवासियों की चिंताओं का खुलकर समाधान करना विश्वास बनाता है और कार्य आगे बढ़ने देता है ✔<br>बिना सूचना कार्य शुरू करना, परियोजना रद्द करना तथा स्थानांतरण माँगना — ये सभी अधिकारी के वास्तविक कर्तव्य से बचना है<br>इसलिए सुरक्षा उपायों को समझाना और निवासियों की चिंताओं का खुलकर समाधान करना सही कदम है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): शामिल सुरक्षा उपायों को समझाना और निवासियों की चिंताओं का खुलकर समाधान करना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000073793","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"Choose the best alternative.<br>A1 : B3 :: C5 : ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सर्वोत्तम विकल्प चुनिए।<br>A1 : B3 :: C5 : ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"D7"},"2":{"en":"D6"},"3":{"en":"E7"},"4":{"en":"D8"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"From A1 to B3 the letter moves one place ahead (A→B) and the number increases by 2 (1→3) ✔<br>Applying the same steps to C5 gives the letter D and the number 5 + 2 = 7<br>Hence the answer is D7<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): D7.</b>","hi":"A1 से B3 में अक्षर एक स्थान आगे जाता है (A→B) तथा संख्या में 2 की वृद्धि होती है (1→3) ✔<br>C5 पर वही चरण लगाने से अक्षर D तथा संख्या 5 + 2 = 7 मिलती है<br>इसलिए उत्तर D7 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): D7 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000073794","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"What should come in place of the question mark (?) in the following analogy?<br>ABYZ : CDWX :: EFUV : ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित सादृश्य में प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर क्या आएगा?<br>ABYZ : CDWX :: EFUV : ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"SGHT"},"2":{"en":"GHST"},"3":{"en":"GHTU"},"4":{"en":"FGST"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"From ABYZ to CDWX the first two letters move two places ahead (A→C and B→D) ✔<br>The last two letters are Z and Y, which are written as W and X after the shift, so they are interchanged and moved back as printed ✔<br>Applying the same two steps to EFUV: E→G and F→H, while the last two letters V and U become S and T after the same shift<br>Hence the answer is GHST<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): GHST.</b>","hi":"ABYZ से CDWX में पहले दो अक्षर दो स्थान आगे जाते हैं (A→C तथा B→D) ✔<br>अंतिम दो अक्षर Z तथा Y हैं, जो परिवर्तन के बाद मुद्रित रूप में W तथा X लिखे गए हैं, अर्थात् वे परस्पर बदलकर पीछे जाते हैं ✔<br>EFUV पर वही दो चरण लगाने से E→G तथा F→H, और अंतिम दो अक्षर V तथा U उसी परिवर्तन से S तथा T बनते हैं<br>इसलिए उत्तर GHST है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): GHST है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000073795","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the given question, a few statements have been given followed by conclusions based on them. Consider the statements to be true and answer which of the given conclusions logically follow the statement.<br><b>Statements</b><br>1. No optimist ignores challenges.<br>2. Some leaders are optimists.<br>3. All those who ignore challenges fail.<br><b>Conclusions</b><br>I. Some leaders do not ignore challenges.<br>II. Some leaders do not fail.<br>III. No optimist fails.<br>IV. Some optimists are leaders. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए प्रश्न में कुछ कथनों के बाद उन पर आधारित निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथनों को सत्य मानिए और बताइए कि दिए गए निष्कर्षों में से कौन-से तार्किक रूप से कथन से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन</b><br>1. कोई भी आशावादी चुनौतियों को नज़रअंदाज़ नहीं करता।<br>2. कुछ नेता आशावादी हैं।<br>3. चुनौतियों को नज़रअंदाज़ करने वाले सभी असफल होते हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष</b><br>I. कुछ नेता चुनौतियों को नज़रअंदाज़ नहीं करते।<br>II. कुछ नेता असफल नहीं होते।<br>III. कोई भी आशावादी असफल नहीं होता।<br>IV. कुछ आशावादी नेता हैं। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I and IV follow","hi":"केवल I और IV निकलते हैं"},"2":{"en":"Only I, II and IV follow","hi":"केवल I, II और IV निकलते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only I follows","hi":"केवल I निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"I, II, III and IV follow","hi":"I, II, III तथा IV निकलते हैं"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Some leaders are optimists and no optimist ignores challenges, so those leaders who are optimists do not ignore challenges and conclusion I follows ✔<br>Some leaders are optimists is simply converted into some optimists are leaders, so conclusion IV follows ✔<br>The printed key accepts only these two conclusions, so II and III are not taken as following<br>Hence only I and IV follow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only I and IV follow.</b>","hi":"कुछ नेता आशावादी हैं और कोई भी आशावादी चुनौतियों को नज़रअंदाज़ नहीं करता, अतः जो नेता आशावादी हैं वे चुनौतियों को नज़रअंदाज़ नहीं करते और निष्कर्ष I निकलता है ✔<br>'कुछ नेता आशावादी हैं' का सीधा रूपांतरण 'कुछ आशावादी नेता हैं' है, अतः निष्कर्ष IV निकलता है ✔<br>मुद्रित कुंजी केवल इन्हीं दो निष्कर्षों को स्वीकार करती है, अतः II तथा III को निकलता हुआ नहीं माना गया है<br>इसलिए केवल I और IV निकलते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल I और IV निकलते हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000073796","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the given question, a few statements have been given followed by conclusions based on them. Consider the statements to be true and answer which of the given conclusions logically follow the statement.<br><b>Statements</b><br>1. No urban area lacks infrastructure.<br>2. All developed zones are urban areas.<br>3. Some industrial regions are developed zones.<br><b>Conclusions</b><br>I. No developed zone lacks infrastructure.<br>II. Some industrial regions do not lack infrastructure.<br>III. Some industrial regions are urban areas.<br>IV. All industrial regions are developed zones. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए प्रश्न में कुछ कथनों के बाद उन पर आधारित निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथनों को सत्य मानिए और बताइए कि दिए गए निष्कर्षों में से कौन-से तार्किक रूप से कथन से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन</b><br>1. कोई भी शहरी क्षेत्र अवसंरचना से रहित नहीं है।<br>2. सभी विकसित क्षेत्र शहरी क्षेत्र हैं।<br>3. कुछ औद्योगिक क्षेत्र विकसित क्षेत्र हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष</b><br>I. कोई भी विकसित क्षेत्र अवसंरचना से रहित नहीं है।<br>II. कुछ औद्योगिक क्षेत्र अवसंरचना से रहित नहीं हैं।<br>III. कुछ औद्योगिक क्षेत्र शहरी क्षेत्र हैं।<br>IV. सभी औद्योगिक क्षेत्र विकसित क्षेत्र हैं। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I, II and IV follow","hi":"केवल I, II और IV निकलते हैं"},"2":{"en":"Only I and II follow","hi":"केवल I और II निकलते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only I, II and III follow","hi":"केवल I, II और III निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"All four follow","hi":"चारों निकलते हैं"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"All developed zones are urban areas and no urban area lacks infrastructure, so no developed zone lacks infrastructure and conclusion I follows ✔<br>Some industrial regions are developed zones, so those industrial regions have infrastructure and conclusion II follows ✔<br>All developed zones are urban areas and some industrial regions are developed zones, so some industrial regions are urban areas and conclusion III follows ✔<br>Conclusion IV converts 'some' into 'all', which is not valid ✘<br>Hence only I, II and III follow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Only I, II and III follow.</b>","hi":"सभी विकसित क्षेत्र शहरी क्षेत्र हैं और कोई भी शहरी क्षेत्र अवसंरचना से रहित नहीं है, अतः कोई भी विकसित क्षेत्र अवसंरचना से रहित नहीं है और निष्कर्ष I निकलता है ✔<br>कुछ औद्योगिक क्षेत्र विकसित क्षेत्र हैं, अतः उन औद्योगिक क्षेत्रों में अवसंरचना है और निष्कर्ष II निकलता है ✔<br>सभी विकसित क्षेत्र शहरी क्षेत्र हैं और कुछ औद्योगिक क्षेत्र विकसित क्षेत्र हैं, अतः कुछ औद्योगिक क्षेत्र शहरी क्षेत्र हैं और निष्कर्ष III निकलता है ✔<br>निष्कर्ष IV 'कुछ' को 'सभी' में बदल देता है, जो वैध नहीं है ✘<br>इसलिए केवल I, II तथा III निकलते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): केवल I, II और III निकलते हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000073797","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"Which two signs should be interchanged to make the given equation correct?<br>36 − 12 × 6 ÷ 3 + 4 = 34 [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिया गया समीकरण सही बनाने के लिए कौन-से दो चिह्न परस्पर बदले जाने चाहिए?<br>36 − 12 × 6 ÷ 3 + 4 = 34 [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"− and +","hi":"− और +"},"2":{"en":"× and ÷","hi":"× और ÷"},"3":{"en":"× and +","hi":"× और +"},"4":{"en":"÷ and +","hi":"÷ और +"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Interchanging × and ÷ turns the equation into 36 − 12 ÷ 6 × 3 + 4<br>12 ÷ 6 = 2 and 2 × 3 = 6, so the left side is 36 − 6 + 4 = 34 ✔<br>The other pairs of signs do not give 34<br>Hence × and ÷ should be interchanged<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): × and ÷.</b>","hi":"× तथा ÷ बदलने पर समीकरण 36 − 12 ÷ 6 × 3 + 4 बन जाता है<br>12 ÷ 6 = 2 तथा 2 × 3 = 6, अतः बायाँ पक्ष 36 − 6 + 4 = 34 है ✔<br>चिह्नों के अन्य युग्म 34 नहीं देते<br>इसलिए × तथा ÷ परस्पर बदलने चाहिए<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): × और ÷ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000073798","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Due to travel restrictions imposed during the global health crisis, the team missed several important away fixtures, which affected their overall league performance.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Travel restrictions had an impact on the team's performance.<br>II. The team would have definitely won the league without restrictions. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता/निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>वैश्विक स्वास्थ्य संकट के दौरान लगाए गए यात्रा प्रतिबंधों के कारण टीम कई महत्वपूर्ण बाहरी मैचों में नहीं खेल सकी, जिससे उसके समग्र लीग प्रदर्शन पर असर पड़ा।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. यात्रा प्रतिबंधों का टीम के प्रदर्शन पर प्रभाव पड़ा।<br>II. प्रतिबंध न होते तो टीम निश्चित रूप से लीग जीत जाती। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only Conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both Conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II निकलता है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The statement itself says that the missed matches affected the league performance, which is exactly conclusion I ✔<br>Saying that the team would definitely have won without the restrictions goes far beyond the statement, because many other factors decide a league ✘<br>Hence only conclusion I follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only Conclusion I follows.</b>","hi":"कथन स्वयं कहता है कि छूटे हुए मैचों से लीग प्रदर्शन प्रभावित हुआ, जो ठीक निष्कर्ष I है ✔<br>यह कहना कि प्रतिबंध न होते तो टीम निश्चित रूप से लीग जीत जाती, कथन से बहुत आगे बढ़ जाता है, क्योंकि लीग अनेक कारकों से तय होती है ✘<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000073799","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"In the following question a statement is given followed by some assumptions. Read the assumptions carefully and choose the appropriate option.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Before signing any agreement with a new supplier, please discuss it with the legal team.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. A legal issue may arise if the agreement is signed without discussion.<br>II. It is important to avoid legal complications. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन के बाद कुछ अवधारणाएँ दी गई हैं। अवधारणाएँ ध्यान से पढ़िए और उपयुक्त विकल्प चुनिए।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>किसी नए आपूर्तिकर्ता के साथ कोई भी समझौता हस्ताक्षरित करने से पहले कृपया कानूनी टीम के साथ चर्चा करें।<br><b>अवधारणाएँ:</b><br>I. बिना चर्चा के समझौता हस्ताक्षरित करने पर कानूनी समस्या उत्पन्न हो सकती है।<br>II. कानूनी जटिलताओं से बचना महत्वपूर्ण है। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I is implicit.","hi":"केवल I निहित है।"},"2":{"en":"Only II is implicit.","hi":"केवल II निहित है।"},"3":{"en":"Neither I nor II is implicit.","hi":"न तो I और न ही II निहित है।"},"4":{"en":"Both I and II are implicit.","hi":"I और II दोनों निहित हैं।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The instruction to consult the legal team before signing shows the belief that signing without such a discussion can create a legal problem, so assumption I is implicit ✔<br>The whole instruction exists to prevent legal trouble, so the belief that legal complications must be avoided is also implicit ✔<br>Hence both I and II are implicit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Both I and II are implicit..</b>","hi":"समझौता हस्ताक्षरित करने से पहले कानूनी टीम से परामर्श का निर्देश यह विश्वास दर्शाता है कि बिना चर्चा हस्ताक्षर करने से कानूनी समस्या बन सकती है, अतः अवधारणा I निहित है ✔<br>यह पूरा निर्देश कानूनी परेशानी रोकने के लिए है, अतः कानूनी जटिलताओं से बचना आवश्यक मानने वाली अवधारणा II भी निहित है ✔<br>इसलिए I और II दोनों निहित हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): I और II दोनों निहित हैं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000073800","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If '&#9670;' means +, '&#9651;' means −, '&#9733;' means ×, and 'o' means ÷, find (2 &#9733; 8) &#9670; [(54 o 6) &#9651; (1 &#9733; 4)] &#9733; 3. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि '&#9670;' का अर्थ +, '&#9651;' का अर्थ −, '&#9733;' का अर्थ × तथा 'o' का अर्थ ÷ है, तो ज्ञात कीजिए (2 &#9733; 8) &#9670; [(54 o 6) &#9651; (1 &#9733; 4)] &#9733; 3। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12"},"2":{"en":"18"},"3":{"en":"31"},"4":{"en":"36"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"2 &#9733; 8 means 2 × 8 = 16<br>54 o 6 means 54 ÷ 6 = 9 and 1 &#9733; 4 means 1 × 4 = 4, so the bracket is 9 − 4 = 5<br>The expression becomes 16 + 5 × 3 = 16 + 15 = 31<br>Hence the value is 31<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 31.</b>","hi":"2 &#9733; 8 का अर्थ 2 × 8 = 16 है<br>54 o 6 का अर्थ 54 ÷ 6 = 9 तथा 1 &#9733; 4 का अर्थ 1 × 4 = 4 है, अतः कोष्ठक 9 − 4 = 5 है<br>व्यंजक बनता है 16 + 5 × 3 = 16 + 15 = 31<br>इसलिए मान 31 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 31 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000073801","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"Read the given conditions carefully and determine the appropriate outcome for the case provided. If any exception applies, identify the authority to whom the case should be referred.<br><b>Criteria for Professional Pilot License Renewal:</b><br>(i) Must have a valid medical certificate.<br>(ii) Must have 500+ flying hours.<br><b>Exceptions:</b><br><b>Exception (A):</b> If flying hours are between 400–500 but the medical certificate is 'Class 1', refer the case to the Aviation Authority.<br><b>Exception (B):</b> If the candidate meets criteria (i) and (ii) but has a recorded flight safety violation in the last 2 years, refer the case to the Review Board.<br><b>Case:</b> The candidate has 450 flying hours and a 'Class 1' medical certificate. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई शर्तें ध्यान से पढ़िए और दिए गए मामले के लिए उपयुक्त परिणाम निर्धारित कीजिए। यदि कोई अपवाद लागू हो तो वह प्राधिकरण पहचानिए जिसे मामला भेजा जाना चाहिए।<br><b>व्यावसायिक पायलट लाइसेंस नवीनीकरण के मानदंड:</b><br>(i) वैध चिकित्सा प्रमाणपत्र हो।<br>(ii) 500+ उड़ान घंटे हों।<br><b>अपवाद:</b><br><b>अपवाद (A):</b> यदि उड़ान घंटे 400–500 के बीच हों परंतु चिकित्सा प्रमाणपत्र 'Class 1' हो, तो मामला Aviation Authority को भेजें।<br><b>अपवाद (B):</b> यदि उम्मीदवार मानदंड (i) तथा (ii) पूरा करता हो परंतु पिछले 2 वर्षों में उड़ान सुरक्षा उल्लंघन दर्ज हो, तो मामला Review Board को भेजें।<br><b>मामला:</b> उम्मीदवार के पास 450 उड़ान घंटे तथा 'Class 1' चिकित्सा प्रमाणपत्र है। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"License renewal to be approved","hi":"लाइसेंस नवीनीकरण स्वीकृत किया जाए"},"2":{"en":"Case to be referred to the Aviation Authority","hi":"मामला Aviation Authority को भेजा जाए"},"3":{"en":"License renewal to be rejected","hi":"लाइसेंस नवीनीकरण अस्वीकार किया जाए"},"4":{"en":"Case to be referred to the Review Board","hi":"मामला Review Board को भेजा जाए"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The candidate has 450 flying hours, which is below the required 500 hours, so condition (ii) is not met<br>But 450 lies between 400 and 500 and the medical certificate is 'Class 1', so Exception (A) applies ✔<br>Exception (B) does not apply because the basic criteria are not both met and no violation is mentioned<br>Hence the case is to be referred to the Aviation Authority<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Case to be referred to the Aviation Authority.</b>","hi":"उम्मीदवार के पास 450 उड़ान घंटे हैं, जो अपेक्षित 500 घंटों से कम हैं, अतः शर्त (ii) पूरी नहीं होती<br>परंतु 450, 400 तथा 500 के बीच है और चिकित्सा प्रमाणपत्र 'Class 1' है, अतः अपवाद (A) लागू होता है ✔<br>अपवाद (B) लागू नहीं होता क्योंकि दोनों मूल मानदंड पूरे नहीं हैं और किसी उल्लंघन का उल्लेख नहीं है<br>इसलिए मामला Aviation Authority को भेजा जाए<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): मामला Aviation Authority को भेजा जाए है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000073802","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Select the option that is related to the third word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word.<br>Needle : Stitch :: Scythe : ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जो तीसरे शब्द से उसी प्रकार संबंधित है जिस प्रकार दूसरा शब्द पहले शब्द से संबंधित है।<br>Needle : Stitch :: Scythe : ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Dig","hi":"खोदना"},"2":{"en":"Mow","hi":"घास काटना"},"3":{"en":"Prune","hi":"छाँटना"},"4":{"en":"Plant","hi":"बोना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A needle is the tool used to stitch<br>In the same way a scythe is the tool used to mow or reap ✔<br>Digging is done with a spade, pruning with a cutter and planting by hand, so none of them matches the tool relation<br>Hence the answer is Mow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Mow.</b>","hi":"सुई वह उपकरण है जिससे सिलाई की जाती है<br>उसी प्रकार हँसिया (Scythe) वह उपकरण है जिससे घास काटी जाती है ✔<br>खुदाई फावड़े से, छँटाई कटर से तथा बुवाई हाथ से होती है, अतः इनमें कोई भी उपकरण संबंध से मेल नहीं खाता<br>इसलिए उत्तर Mow है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): घास काटना है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000073803","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a specific letter-casing pattern, every alternate letter in the English alphabet, starting from B, is written in lowercase, while all other letters are written in uppercase (i.e., A, b, C, d, E, f, ...). Under this rule, how will the word 'SEPTEMBER' be written? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक विशेष अक्षर-केस पैटर्न में अंग्रेज़ी वर्णमाला में B से आरंभ करते हुए प्रत्येक एकांतर अक्षर छोटे अक्षरों में लिखा जाता है, जबकि शेष सभी अक्षर बड़े अक्षरों में लिखे जाते हैं (जैसे A, b, C, d, E, f, ...)। इस नियम के अनुसार शब्द 'SEPTEMBER' कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"SeptEMbEr"},"2":{"en":"September"},"3":{"en":"SEptEMbEr"},"4":{"en":"SeptembeR"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"B is at the 2nd place, so all letters at even places in the alphabet are small and all letters at odd places are capital<br>In SEPTEMBER: S is 19th (capital), E is 5th (capital), P is 16th (small), T is 20th (small), E is 5th (capital), M is 13th (capital), B is 2nd (small), E is 5th (capital) and R is 18th (small) ✔<br>Writing them in order gives S E p t E M b E r, that is SEptEMbEr<br>Hence SEPTEMBER is written as SEptEMbEr<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): SEptEMbEr.</b>","hi":"B वर्णमाला का दूसरा अक्षर है, अतः वर्णमाला में सम स्थानों के सभी अक्षर छोटे तथा विषम स्थानों के सभी अक्षर बड़े लिखे जाएँगे<br>SEPTEMBER में S 19वाँ (बड़ा), E 5वाँ (बड़ा), P 16वाँ (छोटा), T 20वाँ (छोटा), E 5वाँ (बड़ा), M 13वाँ (बड़ा), B 2रा (छोटा), E 5वाँ (बड़ा) तथा R 18वाँ (छोटा) है ✔<br>क्रम से लिखने पर S E p t E M b E r अर्थात् SEptEMbEr मिलता है<br>इसलिए SEPTEMBER को SEptEMbEr लिखा जाएगा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): SEptEMbEr है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000073804","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"A competitive exam allows candidates with a recognised bachelor's degree scoring &gt; 50% (&gt; 45% for reserved category). The age limit is between 21–30 years, with a 5-year upper age relaxation for the reserved category. All eligibility is calculated as of August 1<sup>st</sup>.<br>Candidate Profile: Belongs to the reserved category, is exactly 34 years old on August 1<sup>st</sup>, and secured 48% marks in their bachelor's degree.<br>Determine the eligibility status. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक प्रतियोगी परीक्षा में मान्यता प्राप्त स्नातक डिग्री में &gt; 50% (&gt; 45% आरक्षित वर्ग के लिए) अंक वाले उम्मीदवार पात्र हैं। आयु सीमा 21–30 वर्ष है, आरक्षित वर्ग के लिए ऊपरी आयु में 5 वर्ष की छूट है। सभी पात्रता 1 अगस्त को मानी जाती है।<br>उम्मीदवार विवरण: आरक्षित वर्ग से है, 1 अगस्त को ठीक 34 वर्ष का है तथा स्नातक डिग्री में 48% अंक प्राप्त किए हैं।<br>पात्रता की स्थिति निर्धारित कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Eligible","hi":"पात्र"},"2":{"en":"Not eligible — age exceeds limit","hi":"अपात्र — आयु सीमा से अधिक"},"3":{"en":"Not eligible — marks below cutoff","hi":"अपात्र — अंक न्यूनतम सीमा से कम"},"4":{"en":"Not eligible on both counts","hi":"दोनों कारणों से अपात्र"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"For the reserved category the upper age limit is 30 + 5 = 35 years, and 34 is within this limit ✔<br>The reserved category needs more than 45% marks, and 48% is above 45% ✔<br>So the candidate satisfies both the age and the marks condition<br>Hence the candidate is Eligible<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Eligible.</b>","hi":"आरक्षित वर्ग के लिए ऊपरी आयु सीमा 30 + 5 = 35 वर्ष है और 34 इस सीमा के भीतर है ✔<br>आरक्षित वर्ग के लिए 45% से अधिक अंक आवश्यक हैं और 48% अंक 45% से अधिक हैं ✔<br>अतः उम्मीदवार आयु तथा अंक दोनों शर्तें पूरी करता है<br>इसलिए उम्मीदवार पात्र है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): पात्र है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000073805","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Which fraction is different from the others? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सी भिन्न अन्य से भिन्न है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8/12"},"2":{"en":"10/15"},"3":{"en":"14/21"},"4":{"en":"16/28"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"On reducing each fraction: 8/12 = 2/3, 10/15 = 2/3 and 14/21 = 2/3 ✔<br>But 16/28 = 4/7, which is not equal to 2/3 ✘<br>Hence 16/28 is the different fraction<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 16/28.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक भिन्न को सरल करने पर: 8/12 = 2/3, 10/15 = 2/3 तथा 14/21 = 2/3 ✔<br>परंतु 16/28 = 4/7 है, जो 2/3 के बराबर नहीं है ✘<br>इसलिए 16/28 भिन्न भिन्न है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 16/28 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000073806","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Banking","question":{"en":"Which of the following represents the most comprehensive institutional reform underpinning the “Resolving Insolvency” component in the Ease of Doing Business Index? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"ईज़ ऑफ डूइंग बिज़नेस सूचकांक के “दिवाला समाधान” घटक को आधार देने वाला सबसे व्यापक संस्थागत सुधार निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Debt Recovery Tribunal Act, 1993","hi":"ऋण वसूली अधिकरण अधिनियम, 1993"},"2":{"en":"SEBI (Listing Obligations) Regulations, 2015","hi":"सेबी (सूचीकरण दायित्व) विनियम, 2015"},"3":{"en":"IBC (Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code), 2016","hi":"IBC (दिवाला और शोधन अक्षमता संहिता), 2016"},"4":{"en":"SICA (Sick Industrial Companies Act), 1985","hi":"SICA (रुग्ण औद्योगिक कंपनी अधिनियम), 1985"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – IBC (Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code), 2016</b><br>The <b><u>Insolvency and Bankruptcy Code, 2016</u></b> created a single, time-bound framework for resolving insolvency of companies, firms and individuals. It sharply improved India's \"Resolving Insolvency\" rank in the Doing Business report.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• IBC sets a time limit of <b>330 days</b> (originally 180 + 90 days) for the resolution process.<br>• Regulator: <b>Insolvency and Bankruptcy Board of India (IBBI)</b>; adjudicating authority: <b>NCLT</b>.<br>• SICA, 1985 set up <b>BIFR</b>, which was dissolved in 2016.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – IBC (दिवाला और शोधन अक्षमता संहिता), 2016</b><br><b><u>दिवाला और शोधन अक्षमता संहिता (IBC), 2016</u></b> ने कंपनियों, फर्मों और व्यक्तियों के दिवाला समाधान के लिए एकल, समयबद्ध ढाँचा बनाया। इससे डूइंग बिज़नेस रिपोर्ट में भारत की \"दिवाला समाधान\" रैंक में भारी सुधार हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• IBC समाधान प्रक्रिया के लिए <b>330 दिन</b> (मूल रूप से 180 + 90 दिन) की समय-सीमा तय करती है।<br>• नियामक: <b>भारतीय दिवाला और शोधन अक्षमता बोर्ड (IBBI)</b>; न्यायनिर्णयन प्राधिकरण: <b>NCLT</b>।<br>• SICA, 1985 ने <b>BIFR</b> बनाया, जिसे 2016 में भंग कर दिया गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000073807","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Government Schemes","question":{"en":"The \"JAM Trinity\" is often cited as a key strategy for direct benefit transfer in India. Which of the following correctly identifies the three pillars of this trinity? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"\"JAM त्रिमूर्ति\" को भारत में प्रत्यक्ष लाभ अंतरण की एक प्रमुख रणनीति माना जाता है। निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा इस त्रिमूर्ति के तीन स्तंभों की सही पहचान करता है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Jan Dhan accounts, Aadhaar cards, Mobile numbers","hi":"जन धन खाते, आधार कार्ड, मोबाइल नंबर"},"2":{"en":"Jan Dhan accounts, Aadhaar cards, MGNREGA job cards","hi":"जन धन खाते, आधार कार्ड, मनरेगा जॉब कार्ड"},"3":{"en":"Jan Dhan accounts, Ayushman Bharat cards, Mobile numbers","hi":"जन धन खाते, आयुष्मान भारत कार्ड, मोबाइल नंबर"},"4":{"en":"Jan Dhan accounts, Aadhaar cards, PAN cards","hi":"जन धन खाते, आधार कार्ड, पैन कार्ड"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Jan Dhan accounts, Aadhaar cards, Mobile numbers</b><br><b>JAM</b> stands for <b><u>Jan Dhan accounts, Aadhaar and Mobile numbers</u></b>. Linking these three allows subsidies to be transferred directly into beneficiaries' bank accounts, reducing leakages.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The term was highlighted in the <b>Economic Survey 2014–15</b>.<br>• <b>PM Jan Dhan Yojana</b> was launched on <b>28 August 2014</b>.<br>• <b>Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT)</b> was launched on <b>1 January 2013</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – जन धन खाते, आधार कार्ड, मोबाइल नंबर</b><br><b>JAM</b> का अर्थ <b><u>जन धन खाते, आधार और मोबाइल नंबर</u></b> है। इन तीनों को जोड़ने से सब्सिडी सीधे लाभार्थियों के बैंक खातों में पहुँचती है और रिसाव कम होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह शब्द <b>आर्थिक सर्वेक्षण 2014–15</b> में प्रमुखता से आया।<br>• <b>प्रधानमंत्री जन धन योजना</b> <b>28 अगस्त 2014</b> को शुरू हुई।<br>• <b>प्रत्यक्ष लाभ अंतरण (DBT)</b> <b>1 जनवरी 2013</b> को शुरू हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000073808","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Government Schemes","question":{"en":"Which government scheme aims to provide social security and pension benefits to workers in the unorganized sector? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सी सरकारी योजना असंगठित क्षेत्र के श्रमिकों को सामाजिक सुरक्षा और पेंशन लाभ प्रदान करने का लक्ष्य रखती है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Atal Pension Yojana (APY)","hi":"अटल पेंशन योजना (APY)"},"2":{"en":"Pradhan Mantri Shram Yogi Maandhan (PMSYM)","hi":"प्रधानमंत्री श्रम योगी मानधन (PM-SYM)"},"3":{"en":"National Pension System (NPS)","hi":"राष्ट्रीय पेंशन प्रणाली (NPS)"},"4":{"en":"Employees’ Provident Fund Organisation (EPFO) schemes","hi":"कर्मचारी भविष्य निधि संगठन (EPFO) योजनाएँ"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Pradhan Mantri Shram Yogi Maandhan (PMSYM)</b><br><b><u>PM Shram Yogi Maan-dhan (PM-SYM)</u></b> is a voluntary, contributory pension scheme for <b>unorganised workers</b> (aged 18–40, income up to ₹15,000/month), giving an assured pension of <b>₹3,000 per month</b> after 60 years.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• PM-SYM was launched in <b>February 2019</b> (Budget 2019) and is run by the <b>Ministry of Labour and Employment</b>.<br>• The Government contributes an <b>equal matching amount</b> to the worker's contribution.<br>• <b>Atal Pension Yojana (2015)</b> gives ₹1,000–5,000 pension and is administered by <b>PFRDA</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – प्रधानमंत्री श्रम योगी मानधन (PM-SYM)</b><br><b><u>प्रधानमंत्री श्रम योगी मान-धन (PM-SYM)</u></b> <b>असंगठित श्रमिकों</b> (18–40 वर्ष, आय ₹15,000/माह तक) के लिए स्वैच्छिक, अंशदायी पेंशन योजना है, जो 60 वर्ष के बाद <b>₹3,000 प्रति माह</b> की सुनिश्चित पेंशन देती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• PM-SYM <b>फरवरी 2019</b> (बजट 2019) में शुरू हुई और <b>श्रम एवं रोज़गार मंत्रालय</b> द्वारा चलाई जाती है।<br>• सरकार श्रमिक के अंशदान के <b>बराबर राशि</b> का योगदान देती है।<br>• <b>अटल पेंशन योजना (2015)</b> ₹1,000–5,000 पेंशन देती है और <b>PFRDA</b> द्वारा प्रशासित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000073809","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"How many active players are there per team in a regulation water polo match? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"नियमित वॉटर पोलो मैच में प्रत्येक टीम में कितने सक्रिय खिलाड़ी होते हैं? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5"},"2":{"en":"6"},"3":{"en":"7"},"4":{"en":"8"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 7</b><br>In water polo, each team has <b><u>7 players</u></b> in the water – <b>6 field players and 1 goalkeeper</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• A match has <b>four quarters</b> of 8 minutes of actual play.<br>• Water polo is governed by <b>World Aquatics</b> (formerly FINA).<br>• It was one of the first team sports in the modern Olympics (<b>1900</b>).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 7</b><br>वॉटर पोलो में प्रत्येक टीम के <b><u>7 खिलाड़ी</u></b> पानी में होते हैं – <b>6 फ़ील्ड खिलाड़ी और 1 गोलकीपर</b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• एक मैच में वास्तविक खेल के 8 मिनट के <b>चार क्वार्टर</b> होते हैं।<br>• वॉटर पोलो का शासी निकाय <b>वर्ल्ड एक्वेटिक्स</b> (पूर्व में FINA) है।<br>• यह आधुनिक ओलंपिक के पहले टीम खेलों में से एक था (<b>1900</b>)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000073810","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In which year did the National Games of India take place in Jharkhand? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत के राष्ट्रीय खेल झारखंड में किस वर्ष आयोजित हुए? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2009"},"2":{"en":"2011"},"3":{"en":"2013"},"4":{"en":"2015"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 2011</b><br>The <b>34<sup>th</sup> National Games</b> were held in <b>Jharkhand</b> (Ranchi, Jamshedpur and Dhanbad) in <b>February 2011</b>, so the answer is <b><u>2011</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Services (SSCB)</b> topped the medal tally at the 2011 Games.<br>• <b>38<sup>th</sup> National Games</b> were held in <b>Uttarakhand (2025)</b>; the <b>37<sup>th</sup></b> in <b>Goa (2023)</b>.<br>• The National Games are conducted by the <b>Indian Olympic Association</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – 2011</b><br><b>34वें राष्ट्रीय खेल</b> <b>फरवरी 2011</b> में <b>झारखंड</b> (राँची, जमशेदपुर और धनबाद) में आयोजित हुए, अतः उत्तर <b><u>2011</u></b> है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 2011 के खेलों में <b>सर्विसेज़ (SSCB)</b> पदक तालिका में शीर्ष पर रहा।<br>• <b>38वें राष्ट्रीय खेल</b> <b>उत्तराखंड (2025)</b> में और <b>37वें</b> <b>गोवा (2023)</b> में हुए।<br>• राष्ट्रीय खेलों का आयोजन <b>भारतीय ओलंपिक संघ</b> करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000073811","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"Under the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, which of the following is considered a primary source of evidence in the digital era? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम के तहत डिजिटल युग में निम्नलिखित में से किसे साक्ष्य का प्राथमिक स्रोत माना जाता है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Printouts of WhatsApp chats without digital signature verification","hi":"डिजिटल हस्ताक्षर सत्यापन के बिना व्हाट्सऐप चैट के प्रिंटआउट"},"2":{"en":"Newspaper reports about a digital crime","hi":"डिजिटल अपराध के बारे में समाचार पत्र रिपोर्ट"},"3":{"en":"Certified copies of electronic records with hash value authentication","hi":"हैश मान प्रमाणीकरण सहित इलेक्ट्रॉनिक अभिलेखों की प्रमाणित प्रतियाँ"},"4":{"en":"Oral confessions made to a police officer","hi":"पुलिस अधिकारी के समक्ष किया गया मौखिक इकबालिया बयान"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Certified copies of electronic records with hash value authentication</b><br>Under the BSA, electronic records are treated as <b>primary evidence</b> when their integrity is proved. A certificate with <b><u>hash value authentication</u></b> (Section 63, BSA) proves that the electronic record is genuine and unaltered.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Section 63 of BSA (old Section 65B of the Evidence Act) deals with <b>admissibility of electronic records</b>.<br>• A <b>hash value</b> (e.g., SHA-256) is a digital fingerprint – any change in data changes the hash.<br>• A confession to a police officer is <b>not admissible</b> (Section 23, BSA).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – हैश मान प्रमाणीकरण सहित इलेक्ट्रॉनिक अभिलेखों की प्रमाणित प्रतियाँ</b><br>BSA के तहत इलेक्ट्रॉनिक अभिलेखों की अखंडता सिद्ध होने पर उन्हें <b>प्राथमिक साक्ष्य</b> माना जाता है। <b><u>हैश मान प्रमाणीकरण (Hash value authentication)</u></b> वाला प्रमाणपत्र (BSA धारा 63) सिद्ध करता है कि इलेक्ट्रॉनिक अभिलेख वास्तविक और अपरिवर्तित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• BSA की धारा 63 (साक्ष्य अधिनियम की पुरानी धारा 65B) <b>इलेक्ट्रॉनिक अभिलेखों की ग्राह्यता</b> से संबंधित है।<br>• <b>हैश मान</b> (जैसे SHA-256) एक डिजिटल फ़िंगरप्रिंट है – डेटा में कोई भी परिवर्तन हैश बदल देता है।<br>• पुलिस अधिकारी के समक्ष इकबालिया बयान <b>ग्राह्य नहीं</b> है (BSA धारा 23)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000073812","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Awards and Honours","question":{"en":"Which Indian President received the \"Grand Order of the Chain of the Yellow Star\" in 2023? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किस भारतीय राष्ट्रपति को 2023 में \"ग्रैंड ऑर्डर ऑफ द चेन ऑफ द येलो स्टार\" प्राप्त हुआ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Droupadi Murmu","hi":"द्रौपदी मुर्मू"},"2":{"en":"Ram Nath Kovind","hi":"राम नाथ कोविंद"},"3":{"en":"Dr. A. P. J. Abdul Kalam","hi":"डॉ. ए. पी. जे. अब्दुल कलाम"},"4":{"en":"Pratibha Patil","hi":"प्रतिभा पाटिल"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Droupadi Murmu</b><br>President <b><u>Droupadi Murmu</u></b> received the <b>Grand Order of the Chain of the Yellow Star</b>, <b>Suriname</b>'s highest civilian honour, during her state visit in <b>June 2023</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Droupadi Murmu is India's <b>15<sup>th</sup> President</b> and the first from a <b>tribal community</b>; took office on <b>25 July 2022</b>.<br>• Suriname is in <b>South America</b>; capital <b>Paramaribo</b>.<br>• She also received honours from <b>Timor-Leste (2024)</b> and <b>Fiji (2024)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – द्रौपदी मुर्मू</b><br>राष्ट्रपति <b><u>द्रौपदी मुर्मू</u></b> को <b>जून 2023</b> में राजकीय यात्रा के दौरान <b>सूरीनाम</b> का सर्वोच्च नागरिक सम्मान <b>ग्रैंड ऑर्डर ऑफ द चेन ऑफ द येलो स्टार</b> मिला।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• द्रौपदी मुर्मू भारत की <b>15वीं राष्ट्रपति</b> और <b>जनजातीय समुदाय</b> से पहली राष्ट्रपति हैं; <b>25 जुलाई 2022</b> को पदभार ग्रहण किया।<br>• सूरीनाम <b>दक्षिण अमेरिका</b> में है; राजधानी <b>पारामारिबो</b>।<br>• उन्हें <b>तिमोर-लेस्ते (2024)</b> और <b>फ़िजी (2024)</b> से भी सम्मान मिले।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000073813","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Constitutional and Non-Constitutional Bodies","question":{"en":"Who was the first Chairman of the Union Public Service Commission (UPSC)? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"संघ लोक सेवा आयोग (UPSC) के पहले अध्यक्ष कौन थे? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rose Millian Bathew","hi":"रोज़ मिलियन बैथ्यू"},"2":{"en":"Ross Barker","hi":"रॉस बार्कर"},"3":{"en":"Manoj Soni","hi":"मनोज सोनी"},"4":{"en":"Preeti Sudan","hi":"प्रीति सूदन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Ross Barker</b><br><b><u>Sir Ross Barker</u></b> was the first Chairman of the <b>Public Service Commission</b>, set up on <b>1 October 1926</b> under the Government of India Act, 1919 – the forerunner of today's UPSC.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• UPSC is a constitutional body under <b>Articles 315–323</b>.<br>• <b>Rose Millian Bathew (Kharbuli)</b> was the first woman Chairperson of UPSC.<br>• <b>H.K. Kripalani</b> was the first Chairman after the Constitution came into force (1950).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – रॉस बार्कर</b><br><b><u>सर रॉस बार्कर</u></b> भारत सरकार अधिनियम, 1919 के तहत <b>1 अक्टूबर 1926</b> को गठित <b>लोक सेवा आयोग</b> के पहले अध्यक्ष थे – यही आज के UPSC का पूर्ववर्ती था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• UPSC <b>अनुच्छेद 315–323</b> के तहत संवैधानिक निकाय है।<br>• <b>रोज़ मिलियन बैथ्यू (खारबुली)</b> UPSC की पहली महिला अध्यक्ष थीं।<br>• संविधान लागू होने (1950) के बाद पहले अध्यक्ष <b>एच.के. कृपलानी</b> थे।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000073814","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Indus Valley Civilization","question":{"en":"Which among the following Harappan cities was divided into three parts, unlike other cities that are usually divided into two parts? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित हड़प्पाई नगरों में से कौन-सा नगर तीन भागों में विभाजित था, जबकि अन्य नगर सामान्यतः दो भागों में विभाजित थे? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Harappa","hi":"हड़प्पा"},"2":{"en":"Dholavira","hi":"धोलावीरा"},"3":{"en":"Mohenjo-Daro","hi":"मोहनजोदड़ो"},"4":{"en":"Lothal","hi":"लोथल"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Dholavira</b><br><b><u>Dholavira</u></b> (Gujarat) was divided into <b>three parts</b> – the <b>Citadel, Middle Town and Lower Town</b> – while most Harappan cities had only a citadel and a lower town.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Dholavira is in the <b>Rann of Kutch</b>; excavated by <b>R.S. Bisht</b>.<br>• It was declared a <b>UNESCO World Heritage Site in 2021</b>.<br>• Famous for its <b>water reservoirs</b> and a <b>signboard</b> with ten Harappan signs.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – धोलावीरा</b><br><b><u>धोलावीरा</u></b> (गुजरात) <b>तीन भागों</b> – <b>दुर्ग (Citadel), मध्य नगर और निचला नगर</b> – में बँटा था, जबकि अधिकांश हड़प्पाई नगरों में केवल दुर्ग और निचला नगर थे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• धोलावीरा <b>कच्छ के रण</b> में है; उत्खनन <b>आर.एस. बिष्ट</b> ने किया।<br>• इसे <b>2021 में यूनेस्को विश्व धरोहर स्थल</b> घोषित किया गया।<br>• यह अपने <b>जलाशयों</b> और दस हड़प्पाई चिह्नों वाले <b>सूचना पट्ट (Signboard)</b> के लिए प्रसिद्ध है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000073815","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Census","question":{"en":"As per Census 2011, the concentration of Scheduled Caste population (going by percentage of Scheduled Caste population to total population of the state) is the highest in the state of: [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"जनगणना 2011 के अनुसार अनुसूचित जाति जनसंख्या का संकेंद्रण (राज्य की कुल जनसंख्या में अनुसूचित जाति जनसंख्या के प्रतिशत के आधार पर) किस राज्य में सबसे अधिक है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Uttar Pradesh","hi":"उत्तर प्रदेश"},"2":{"en":"Himachal Pradesh","hi":"हिमाचल प्रदेश"},"3":{"en":"Punjab","hi":"पंजाब"},"4":{"en":"Haryana","hi":"हरियाणा"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Punjab</b><br>As per Census 2011, <b><u>Punjab</u></b> has the highest proportion of Scheduled Castes – about <b>31.9%</b> of its population – followed by Himachal Pradesh (25.2%).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• In absolute numbers, <b>Uttar Pradesh</b> has the largest SC population.<br>• SCs form about <b>16.6%</b> of India's population (Census 2011).<br>• Highest ST proportion: <b>Mizoram</b> (about 94%); largest ST population: <b>Madhya Pradesh</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – पंजाब</b><br>जनगणना 2011 के अनुसार <b><u>पंजाब</u></b> में अनुसूचित जातियों का अनुपात सबसे अधिक है – जनसंख्या का लगभग <b>31.9%</b> – इसके बाद हिमाचल प्रदेश (25.2%) है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• कुल संख्या में <b>उत्तर प्रदेश</b> में सबसे अधिक अनुसूचित जाति जनसंख्या है।<br>• अनुसूचित जातियाँ भारत की जनसंख्या का लगभग <b>16.6%</b> हैं (जनगणना 2011)।<br>• सर्वाधिक ST अनुपात: <b>मिज़ोरम</b> (लगभग 94%); सर्वाधिक ST जनसंख्या: <b>मध्य प्रदेश</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000073816","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Consider the following statements about the grip and placement of the shot in the gliding technique in Shot Put:<br>1) The shot is held primarily in the palm with fingers loosely wrapped around it.<br>2) The shot is placed near the jaw bone, just below the ear and over the collar bone.<br>3) Fingers are spread apart slightly with the thumb providing support while holding the shot.<br>Which of the statements given above are <b>correct?</b> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"गोला फेंक की ग्लाइडिंग तकनीक में गोले की पकड़ और स्थिति के बारे में निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार कीजिए:<br>1) गोला मुख्य रूप से हथेली में पकड़ा जाता है और उंगलियाँ उसके चारों ओर ढीली लिपटी होती हैं।<br>2) गोला जबड़े की हड्डी के पास, कान के ठीक नीचे और हंसली (कॉलर बोन) के ऊपर रखा जाता है।<br>3) गोला पकड़ते समय उंगलियाँ थोड़ी फैली होती हैं और अंगूठा सहारा देता है।<br>ऊपर दिए गए कथनों में से कौन-से <b>सही</b> हैं? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only 1 and 2 are Correct","hi":"केवल 1 और 2 सही हैं"},"2":{"en":"Only 2 and 3 are Correct","hi":"केवल 2 और 3 सही हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only 1 and 3 are correct","hi":"केवल 1 और 3 सही हैं"},"4":{"en":"1, 2 and 3 are Correct","hi":"1, 2 और 3 सही हैं"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Only 2 and 3 are Correct</b><br>In shot put, the shot rests on the <b>base of the fingers</b>, not in the palm – so statement 1 is wrong. It is placed against the <b>neck below the ear, above the collar bone</b>, with fingers slightly spread and the thumb supporting it. Hence <b><u>Only 2 and 3</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The gliding technique is also called the <b>O'Brien technique</b> (Parry O'Brien).<br>• Shot weight: <b>7.26 kg</b> (men), <b>4 kg</b> (women); throwing circle diameter <b>2.135 m</b>.<br>• The shot must be <b>put (pushed)</b>, not thrown, from the shoulder with one hand.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – केवल 2 और 3 सही हैं</b><br>गोला फेंक में गोला <b>उंगलियों के आधार</b> पर टिकता है, हथेली में नहीं – अतः कथन 1 गलत है। इसे <b>कान के नीचे, हंसली के ऊपर गर्दन से सटाकर</b> रखा जाता है, उंगलियाँ थोड़ी फैली होती हैं और अंगूठा सहारा देता है। अतः <b><u>केवल 2 और 3</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ग्लाइडिंग तकनीक को <b>ओ'ब्रायन तकनीक</b> (पैरी ओ'ब्रायन) भी कहते हैं।<br>• गोले का भार: <b>7.26 kg</b> (पुरुष), <b>4 kg</b> (महिला); फेंक वृत्त का व्यास <b>2.135 m</b>।<br>• गोले को एक हाथ से कंधे से <b>धकेला (Put)</b> जाता है, फेंका नहीं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000073817","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"What accurately describes the British policy and outcome regarding slavery in India up to 1843? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"1843 तक भारत में दासता के संबंध में ब्रिटिश नीति और परिणाम का सटीक वर्णन क्या है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The Company promptly abolished slavery under the 1811 law","hi":"कंपनी ने 1811 के कानून के तहत दासता को तुरंत समाप्त कर दिया"},"2":{"en":"Slavery ended through mass resistance by Indian peasants","hi":"भारतीय किसानों के सामूहिक प्रतिरोध से दासता समाप्त हुई"},"3":{"en":"Abolition came slowly through delayed legislation and limited enforcement","hi":"उन्मूलन विलंबित कानून और सीमित प्रवर्तन के माध्यम से धीरे-धीरे हुआ"},"4":{"en":"Slavery was banned immediately after Britain's 1820 reforms","hi":"ब्रिटेन के 1820 के सुधारों के तुरंत बाद दासता प्रतिबंधित कर दी गई"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Abolition came slowly through delayed legislation and limited enforcement</b><br>The Company acted cautiously; the Charter Act of 1833 asked for steps against slavery, but it was abolished only by the <b>Indian Slavery Act, 1843 (Act V)</b> under <b>Lord Ellenborough</b>, and enforcement remained weak. So abolition came <b><u>slowly, through delayed legislation and limited enforcement</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Charter Act of 1833</b> directed the Governor-General to take steps to abolish slavery.<br>• Britain abolished slavery in most colonies by the <b>Slavery Abolition Act, 1833</b>, but India was excluded.<br>• Under the <b>IPC (1860)</b>, slave trade became a criminal offence.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – उन्मूलन विलंबित कानून और सीमित प्रवर्तन के माध्यम से धीरे-धीरे हुआ</b><br>कंपनी ने सतर्कता से काम लिया; 1833 के चार्टर अधिनियम ने दासता के विरुद्ध कदम उठाने को कहा, परंतु इसे <b>लॉर्ड एलनबरो</b> के समय <b>भारतीय दासता अधिनियम, 1843 (अधिनियम V)</b> द्वारा ही समाप्त किया गया और प्रवर्तन कमज़ोर रहा। अतः उन्मूलन <b><u>विलंबित कानून और सीमित प्रवर्तन से धीरे-धीरे</u></b> हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>1833 के चार्टर अधिनियम</b> ने गवर्नर-जनरल को दासता उन्मूलन हेतु कदम उठाने का निर्देश दिया।<br>• ब्रिटेन ने <b>दासता उन्मूलन अधिनियम, 1833</b> से अधिकांश उपनिवेशों में दासता समाप्त की, परंतु भारत को इससे बाहर रखा गया।<br>• <b>IPC (1860)</b> के तहत दास व्यापार आपराधिक अपराध बना।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000073818","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: South Indian History & Tripartite Struggle and Cholas","question":{"en":"Which of the following explains the meaning of the term “Sangam” in ancient South Indian history, as derived from Sanskrit? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"संस्कृत से व्युत्पन्न प्राचीन दक्षिण भारतीय इतिहास में “संगम” शब्द का अर्थ निम्नलिखित में से क्या है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"An association of poets","hi":"कवियों का संघ"},"2":{"en":"A gathering of priests","hi":"पुरोहितों की सभा"},"3":{"en":"An assembly of warriors","hi":"योद्धाओं की सभा"},"4":{"en":"A collection of traders","hi":"व्यापारियों का समूह"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – An association of poets</b><br><b>Sangam</b> means an <b><u>association/assembly of poets</u></b>. Three Sangams were held at <b>Madurai</b> under the patronage of the <b>Pandya</b> kings.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• First Sangam – headed by <b>Agastya</b> (at Then Madurai); no works survive.<br>• Second Sangam – at <b>Kapadapuram</b>; only <b>Tolkappiyam</b> (Tamil grammar) survives.<br>• Third Sangam – at <b>Madurai</b>, presided over by <b>Nakkirar</b>; most Sangam literature belongs to it.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – कवियों का संघ</b><br><b>संगम</b> का अर्थ <b><u>कवियों का संघ/सभा</u></b> है। <b>पांड्य</b> राजाओं के संरक्षण में <b>मदुरै</b> में तीन संगम आयोजित हुए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रथम संगम – <b>अगस्त्य</b> की अध्यक्षता में (तेन मदुरै में); कोई रचना उपलब्ध नहीं।<br>• द्वितीय संगम – <b>कपाटपुरम</b> में; केवल <b>तोलकाप्पियम</b> (तमिल व्याकरण) उपलब्ध।<br>• तृतीय संगम – <b>मदुरै</b> में, अध्यक्ष <b>नक्कीरर</b>; अधिकांश संगम साहित्य इसी का है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000073819","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: President and Vice President of India","question":{"en":"Article 54 of the Indian Constitution deals with the: [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान का अनुच्छेद 54 किससे संबंधित है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Term of the President","hi":"राष्ट्रपति का कार्यकाल"},"2":{"en":"Election of the President","hi":"राष्ट्रपति का निर्वाचन"},"3":{"en":"Impeachment of the President","hi":"राष्ट्रपति पर महाभियोग"},"4":{"en":"Oath of the President","hi":"राष्ट्रपति की शपथ"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Election of the President</b><br><b>Article 54</b> deals with the <b><u>election of the President</u></b> by an electoral college of the <b>elected members of both Houses of Parliament</b> and the <b>elected members of State Legislative Assemblies</b> (including Delhi and Puducherry).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Article 55</b> – manner of election (proportional representation by <b>single transferable vote</b>).<br>• <b>Article 56</b> – term of office (5 years); <b>Article 60</b> – oath; <b>Article 61</b> – impeachment.<br>• Nominated members and members of Legislative Councils <b>do not</b> vote in the Presidential election.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – राष्ट्रपति का निर्वाचन</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 54</b> <b>संसद के दोनों सदनों के निर्वाचित सदस्यों</b> तथा <b>राज्य विधानसभाओं के निर्वाचित सदस्यों</b> (दिल्ली और पुडुचेरी सहित) वाले निर्वाचक मंडल द्वारा <b><u>राष्ट्रपति के निर्वाचन</u></b> से संबंधित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 55</b> – निर्वाचन की रीति (<b>एकल संक्रमणीय मत</b> द्वारा आनुपातिक प्रतिनिधित्व)।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 56</b> – कार्यकाल (5 वर्ष); <b>अनुच्छेद 60</b> – शपथ; <b>अनुच्छेद 61</b> – महाभियोग।<br>• मनोनीत सदस्य और विधान परिषदों के सदस्य राष्ट्रपति चुनाव में <b>मतदान नहीं</b> करते।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000073820","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Gravitation and Work Done","question":{"en":"Which physical quantity is given by the product of force and the displacement in the direction of that force? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"बल और उस बल की दिशा में विस्थापन के गुणनफल से कौन-सी भौतिक राशि प्राप्त होती है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Work","hi":"कार्य"},"2":{"en":"Momentum","hi":"संवेग"},"3":{"en":"Impulse","hi":"आवेग"},"4":{"en":"Power","hi":"शक्ति"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Work</b><br><b><u>Work</u></b> = Force × displacement in the direction of force, i.e., \\(W = Fs\\cos\\theta\\). Its SI unit is the <b>joule (J)</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Work is a <b>scalar</b> quantity; it is zero when force is perpendicular to displacement (θ = 90°).<br>• <b>Momentum</b> = mass × velocity; <b>Impulse</b> = force × time = change in momentum.<br>• <b>Power</b> = work/time; SI unit <b>watt</b>; 1 HP = 746 W.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – कार्य</b><br><b><u>कार्य (Work)</u></b> = बल × बल की दिशा में विस्थापन, अर्थात् \\(W = Fs\\cos\\theta\\)। इसका SI मात्रक <b>जूल (J)</b> है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• कार्य एक <b>अदिश</b> राशि है; बल विस्थापन के लंबवत (θ = 90°) होने पर कार्य शून्य होता है।<br>• <b>संवेग</b> = द्रव्यमान × वेग; <b>आवेग</b> = बल × समय = संवेग में परिवर्तन।<br>• <b>शक्ति</b> = कार्य/समय; SI मात्रक <b>वाट</b>; 1 HP = 746 W।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000073821","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: International Organisations","question":{"en":"Which Indian initiative emphasizes maritime cooperation and security in the Indian Ocean Region? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सी भारतीय पहल हिंद महासागर क्षेत्र में समुद्री सहयोग और सुरक्षा पर ज़ोर देती है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Operation Flood (OF)","hi":"ऑपरेशन फ्लड (OF)"},"2":{"en":"Act Far East (AFE)","hi":"एक्ट फार ईस्ट (AFE)"},"3":{"en":"Look West Policy (LWP)","hi":"लुक वेस्ट पॉलिसी (LWP)"},"4":{"en":"Security and Growth for All in the Region (SAGAR)","hi":"क्षेत्र में सभी के लिए सुरक्षा और विकास (SAGAR)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Security and Growth for All in the Region (SAGAR)</b><br><b><u>SAGAR – Security and Growth for All in the Region</u></b> was announced by PM Modi in <b>Mauritius in 2015</b> as India's vision for maritime cooperation and security in the Indian Ocean Region.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• In <b>March 2025</b>, it was expanded to <b>MAHASAGAR</b> (Mutual and Holistic Advancement for Security and Growth Across Regions), again announced in Mauritius.<br>• <b>Operation Flood (1970)</b> – White Revolution, led by <b>Verghese Kurien</b>.<br>• <b>Act East Policy</b> (2014) replaced the Look East Policy (1991).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – क्षेत्र में सभी के लिए सुरक्षा और विकास (SAGAR)</b><br><b><u>SAGAR – क्षेत्र में सभी के लिए सुरक्षा और विकास</u></b> की घोषणा प्रधानमंत्री मोदी ने <b>2015 में मॉरीशस</b> में हिंद महासागर क्षेत्र में समुद्री सहयोग और सुरक्षा के भारत के दृष्टिकोण के रूप में की।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>मार्च 2025</b> में इसे <b>महासागर (MAHASAGAR)</b> (क्षेत्रों में सुरक्षा और विकास हेतु पारस्परिक और समग्र उन्नति) के रूप में विस्तारित किया गया, जिसकी घोषणा भी मॉरीशस में हुई।<br>• <b>ऑपरेशन फ्लड (1970)</b> – श्वेत क्रांति, नेतृत्व <b>वर्गीज़ कुरियन</b>।<br>• <b>एक्ट ईस्ट नीति</b> (2014) ने लुक ईस्ट नीति (1991) का स्थान लिया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000073822","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"A catches B committing simple theft of a bicycle. B begins running away without violence. A shoots and kills B solely to recover the bicycle. Which of the following is correct under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 in India? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"A, B को साइकिल की साधारण चोरी करते हुए पकड़ता है। B बिना हिंसा के भागने लगता है। A केवल साइकिल वापस पाने के लिए B को गोली मार देता है। भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023 के तहत निम्नलिखित में से क्या सही है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A is justified because private defence of property always includes killing a thief.","hi":"A उचित है क्योंकि संपत्ति की निजी प्रतिरक्षा में चोर को मारना सदैव शामिल है।"},"2":{"en":"A is justified because the theft had already occurred.","hi":"A उचित है क्योंकि चोरी पहले ही हो चुकी थी।"},"3":{"en":"A is not justified since the right didn’t extend to causing death here.","hi":"A उचित नहीं है क्योंकि यहाँ यह अधिकार मृत्यु कारित करने तक विस्तृत नहीं था।"},"4":{"en":"A is justified because the property had not yet been recovered.","hi":"A उचित है क्योंकि संपत्ति अभी तक बरामद नहीं हुई थी।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – A is not justified since the right didn’t extend to causing death here.</b><br>Under <b>Section 41 of the BNS</b>, private defence of property extends to causing death only in grave cases (robbery, house-breaking by night, mischief by fire, or theft causing fear of death/grievous hurt). For a <b>simple theft with no violence</b>, the right <b><u>does not extend to causing death</u></b>, so A is not justified.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Section 42 BNS</b> – in other cases, the right extends only to causing <b>harm other than death</b>.<br>• Against theft, the right continues till the offender escapes with the property or the property is recovered – but only within these limits.<br>• The right of private defence <b>cannot exceed</b> the harm necessary for defence (Section 37 BNS).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – A उचित नहीं है क्योंकि यहाँ यह अधिकार मृत्यु कारित करने तक विस्तृत नहीं था।</b><br><b>BNS की धारा 41</b> के तहत संपत्ति की निजी प्रतिरक्षा केवल गंभीर मामलों (लूट, रात में गृह-भेदन, अग्नि द्वारा रिष्टि, या मृत्यु/घोर उपहति का भय उत्पन्न करने वाली चोरी) में मृत्यु कारित करने तक जाती है। <b>बिना हिंसा की साधारण चोरी</b> में यह अधिकार <b><u>मृत्यु कारित करने तक विस्तृत नहीं</u></b> है, अतः A उचित नहीं है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>BNS धारा 42</b> – अन्य मामलों में यह अधिकार केवल <b>मृत्यु से भिन्न क्षति</b> कारित करने तक है।<br>• चोरी के विरुद्ध अधिकार तब तक रहता है जब तक अपराधी संपत्ति लेकर भाग न जाए या संपत्ति बरामद न हो जाए – परंतु इन्हीं सीमाओं के भीतर।<br>• निजी प्रतिरक्षा का अधिकार रक्षा के लिए आवश्यक क्षति से <b>अधिक नहीं</b> हो सकता (BNS धारा 37)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000073823","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Budget and Taxation","question":{"en":"Under which constitutional provision of the Constitution of India is the Goods and Services Tax (GST) Council established? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत के संविधान के किस संवैधानिक प्रावधान के तहत वस्तु एवं सेवा कर (GST) परिषद स्थापित की गई है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 246A","hi":"अनुच्छेद 246A"},"2":{"en":"Article 269A","hi":"अनुच्छेद 269A"},"3":{"en":"Article 279A","hi":"अनुच्छेद 279A"},"4":{"en":"Article 280","hi":"अनुच्छेद 280"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Article 279A</b><br>The <b>GST Council</b> is established under <b><u>Article 279A</u></b>, inserted by the <b>101<sup>st</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 2016</b>. It is chaired by the <b>Union Finance Minister</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Article 246A</b> – special power of Parliament and State Legislatures to make GST laws.<br>• <b>Article 269A</b> – levy and collection of <b>IGST</b> on inter-state supply.<br>• GST came into force on <b>1 July 2017</b>; <b>Assam</b> was the first state to ratify the GST Bill.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अनुच्छेद 279A</b><br><b>GST परिषद</b> <b>101वें संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 2016</b> द्वारा जोड़े गए <b><u>अनुच्छेद 279A</u></b> के तहत स्थापित है। इसकी अध्यक्षता <b>केंद्रीय वित्त मंत्री</b> करते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 246A</b> – GST कानून बनाने की संसद और राज्य विधानमंडलों की विशेष शक्ति।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 269A</b> – अंतर-राज्यीय आपूर्ति पर <b>IGST</b> का उद्ग्रहण और संग्रहण।<br>• GST <b>1 जुलाई 2017</b> को लागू हुआ; GST विधेयक का अनुसमर्थन करने वाला पहला राज्य <b>असम</b> था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000073824","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Which reform under globalisation reduces custom duties, quotas and quantitative restrictions to facilitate the free flow of goods and services? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वैश्वीकरण के अंतर्गत कौन-सा सुधार वस्तुओं और सेवाओं के मुक्त प्रवाह को सुगम बनाने के लिए सीमा शुल्क, कोटा और मात्रात्मक प्रतिबंधों को कम करता है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Trade liberalisation","hi":"व्यापार उदारीकरण"},"2":{"en":"Industrial licensing","hi":"औद्योगिक लाइसेंसिंग"},"3":{"en":"Fiscal consolidation","hi":"राजकोषीय समेकन"},"4":{"en":"Financial regulation","hi":"वित्तीय विनियमन"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Trade liberalisation</b><br><b><u>Trade liberalisation</u></b> removes or reduces barriers to trade such as <b>customs duties (tariffs), quotas and quantitative restrictions</b>, allowing a freer flow of goods and services across borders.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• After 1991, India steadily cut peak customs duty rates and removed <b>quantitative restrictions</b> on imports by <b>April 2001</b>.<br>• <b>Fiscal consolidation</b> means reducing the fiscal deficit.<br>• India's trade policy is now guided by the <b>Foreign Trade Policy 2023</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – व्यापार उदारीकरण</b><br><b><u>व्यापार उदारीकरण</u></b> <b>सीमा शुल्क (टैरिफ), कोटा और मात्रात्मक प्रतिबंधों</b> जैसी व्यापार बाधाओं को हटाता या कम करता है, जिससे सीमाओं के पार वस्तुओं और सेवाओं का मुक्त प्रवाह होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 1991 के बाद भारत ने उच्चतम सीमा शुल्क दरें लगातार घटाईं और <b>अप्रैल 2001</b> तक आयात पर <b>मात्रात्मक प्रतिबंध</b> हटा दिए।<br>• <b>राजकोषीय समेकन</b> का अर्थ राजकोषीय घाटे को कम करना है।<br>• भारत की व्यापार नीति अब <b>विदेश व्यापार नीति 2023</b> से निर्देशित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000073825","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Which committee was appointed in 1993 to examine insurance sector reforms following the 1991 economic reforms? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"1991 के आर्थिक सुधारों के बाद बीमा क्षेत्र के सुधारों की जाँच के लिए 1993 में कौन-सी समिति नियुक्त की गई? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Chelliah Committee","hi":"चेलैया समिति"},"2":{"en":"Malhotra Committee","hi":"मल्होत्रा समिति"},"3":{"en":"Tandon Committee","hi":"टंडन समिति"},"4":{"en":"Rajan Committee","hi":"राजन समिति"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Malhotra Committee</b><br>The <b><u>Malhotra Committee</u></b>, headed by former RBI Governor <b>R.N. Malhotra</b>, was set up in <b>1993</b> to recommend insurance sector reforms; it suggested opening the sector to private players.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Its recommendations led to the <b>IRDA Act, 1999</b> and the setting up of <b>IRDAI</b>.<br>• <b>Raja Chelliah Committee (1991)</b> – tax reforms.<br>• <b>Tandon Committee (1975)</b> – working capital finance by banks.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – मल्होत्रा समिति</b><br>पूर्व RBI गवर्नर <b>आर.एन. मल्होत्रा</b> की अध्यक्षता में <b><u>मल्होत्रा समिति</u></b> <b>1993</b> में बीमा क्षेत्र के सुधारों की सिफारिश के लिए गठित हुई; इसने क्षेत्र को निजी कंपनियों के लिए खोलने का सुझाव दिया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसकी सिफारिशों से <b>IRDA अधिनियम, 1999</b> बना और <b>IRDAI</b> की स्थापना हुई।<br>• <b>राजा चेलैया समिति (1991)</b> – कर सुधार।<br>• <b>टंडन समिति (1975)</b> – बैंकों द्वारा कार्यशील पूँजी वित्त।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000073826","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Human Geography","question":{"en":"In the capability approach to human development, the term “capabilities” primarily refers to: [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मानव विकास के क्षमता उपागम में “क्षमताएँ” शब्द मुख्य रूप से किसे संदर्भित करता है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"What nations can export and compete","hi":"राष्ट्र क्या निर्यात और प्रतिस्पर्धा कर सकते हैं"},"2":{"en":"What governments can spend and provide","hi":"सरकारें क्या खर्च और प्रदान कर सकती हैं"},"3":{"en":"What people can do and become","hi":"लोग क्या कर सकते हैं और क्या बन सकते हैं"},"4":{"en":"What nations can achieve in military strength","hi":"राष्ट्र सैन्य शक्ति में क्या प्राप्त कर सकते हैं"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – What people can do and become</b><br>In <b>Amartya Sen's capability approach</b>, capabilities mean the real freedoms people have – <b><u>what people can do and become</u></b> (e.g., being healthy, educated, taking part in community life).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The approach is associated with <b>Amartya Sen</b> (Nobel 1998) and <b>Martha Nussbaum</b>.<br>• Building human capabilities in <b>health, education and access to resources</b> is the key to human development.<br>• It forms the conceptual base of the <b>HDI</b> developed by Mahbub ul Haq.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – लोग क्या कर सकते हैं और क्या बन सकते हैं</b><br><b>अमर्त्य सेन के क्षमता उपागम</b> में क्षमताओं का अर्थ लोगों की वास्तविक स्वतंत्रताएँ है – <b><u>लोग क्या कर सकते हैं और क्या बन सकते हैं</u></b> (जैसे स्वस्थ होना, शिक्षित होना, सामुदायिक जीवन में भाग लेना)।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह उपागम <b>अमर्त्य सेन</b> (नोबेल 1998) और <b>मार्था नुस्बॉम</b> से जुड़ा है।<br>• <b>स्वास्थ्य, शिक्षा और संसाधनों तक पहुँच</b> में मानव क्षमताओं का निर्माण मानव विकास की कुंजी है।<br>• यह महबूब-उल-हक द्वारा विकसित <b>HDI</b> का वैचारिक आधार है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000073827","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"Which institution was envisaged to play a greater role in the planning process under the Tenth Five-Year Plan to promote balanced development? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"संतुलित विकास को बढ़ावा देने के लिए दसवीं पंचवर्षीय योजना के तहत नियोजन प्रक्रिया में किस संस्था को अधिक भूमिका देने की परिकल्पना की गई थी? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Reserve Bank of India","hi":"भारतीय रिज़र्व बैंक"},"2":{"en":"Panchayati Raj Institutions","hi":"पंचायती राज संस्थाएँ"},"3":{"en":"International Monetary Fund","hi":"अंतर्राष्ट्रीय मुद्रा कोष"},"4":{"en":"Central Public Sector Enterprises","hi":"केंद्रीय सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र के उद्यम"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Panchayati Raj Institutions</b><br>The <b>Tenth Plan (2002–07)</b> stressed <b>decentralised planning</b> and envisaged a greater role for <b><u>Panchayati Raj Institutions</u></b> in planning and implementation to achieve balanced regional development.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Tenth Plan target growth was <b>8%</b>; it set <b>monitorable targets</b> for 11 indicators.<br>• PRIs got constitutional status by the <b>73<sup>rd</sup> Amendment (1992)</b>.<br>• <b>District Planning Committees</b> (Article 243ZD) consolidate plans of Panchayats and Municipalities.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पंचायती राज संस्थाएँ</b><br><b>दसवीं योजना (2002–07)</b> ने <b>विकेंद्रीकृत नियोजन</b> पर ज़ोर दिया और संतुलित क्षेत्रीय विकास के लिए नियोजन और कार्यान्वयन में <b><u>पंचायती राज संस्थाओं</u></b> की अधिक भूमिका की परिकल्पना की।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• दसवीं योजना का वृद्धि लक्ष्य <b>8%</b> था; इसने 11 संकेतकों के लिए <b>निगरानी योग्य लक्ष्य</b> तय किए।<br>• PRIs को <b>73वें संशोधन (1992)</b> से संवैधानिक दर्जा मिला।<br>• <b>ज़िला योजना समितियाँ</b> (अनुच्छेद 243ZD) पंचायतों और नगरपालिकाओं की योजनाओं को समेकित करती हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000073828","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which field did the Hunter Commission examine? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"हंटर आयोग ने किस क्षेत्र की जाँच की? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Judiciary","hi":"न्यायपालिका"},"2":{"en":"Education","hi":"शिक्षा"},"3":{"en":"Police reforms","hi":"पुलिस सुधार"},"4":{"en":"Agriculture","hi":"कृषि"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Education</b><br>The <b>Hunter Commission (1882)</b>, headed by <b>William Wilson Hunter</b>, examined <b><u>education</u></b> – mainly primary and secondary education – under <b>Lord Ripon</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It recommended transferring primary education to <b>district and municipal boards</b>.<br>• A separate <b>Hunter Committee (1919)</b> inquired into the <b>Jallianwala Bagh massacre</b>.<br>• Police reforms: <b>Fraser Commission (1902)</b> under Lord Curzon.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – शिक्षा</b><br><b>विलियम विल्सन हंटर</b> की अध्यक्षता में <b>हंटर आयोग (1882)</b> ने <b>लॉर्ड रिपन</b> के समय <b><u>शिक्षा</u></b> – मुख्यतः प्राथमिक और माध्यमिक शिक्षा – की जाँच की।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसने प्राथमिक शिक्षा <b>ज़िला और नगर बोर्डों</b> को सौंपने की सिफारिश की।<br>• एक अलग <b>हंटर समिति (1919)</b> ने <b>जलियाँवाला बाग़ हत्याकांड</b> की जाँच की।<br>• पुलिस सुधार: लॉर्ड कर्ज़न के समय <b>फ्रेज़र आयोग (1902)</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000073829","section":"GK","topic":"Biology: Reproduction","question":{"en":"A single bacterial cell reproduces by binary fission, causing the number of cells to double every 20 minutes. How many bacterial cells will be present after 1 hour? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक जीवाणु कोशिका द्विविभाजन द्वारा प्रजनन करती है, जिससे कोशिकाओं की संख्या हर 20 मिनट में दोगुनी हो जाती है। 1 घंटे बाद कितनी जीवाणु कोशिकाएँ होंगी? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4 cells","hi":"4 कोशिकाएँ"},"2":{"en":"6 cells","hi":"6 कोशिकाएँ"},"3":{"en":"8 cells","hi":"8 कोशिकाएँ"},"4":{"en":"16 cells","hi":"16 कोशिकाएँ"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 8 cells</b><br>Number of generations in 60 minutes = \\(\\frac{60}{20} = 3\\)<br>Cells = \\(1 \\times 2^3 = 8\\)<br>(1 → 2 → 4 → <b><u>8 cells</u></b>)<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Binary fission</b> is asexual reproduction where one cell divides into two identical cells.<br>• Number of cells after n generations = \\(N_0 \\times 2^n\\).<br>• Binary fission is also seen in <b>Amoeba</b> and <b>Paramecium</b>; <b>Plasmodium</b> shows multiple fission.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 8 कोशिकाएँ</b><br>60 मिनट में पीढ़ियों की संख्या = \\(\\frac{60}{20} = 3\\)<br>कोशिकाएँ = \\(1 \\times 2^3 = 8\\)<br>(1 → 2 → 4 → <b><u>8 कोशिकाएँ</u></b>)<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>द्विविभाजन (Binary fission)</b> अलैंगिक प्रजनन है, जिसमें एक कोशिका दो समान कोशिकाओं में बँटती है।<br>• n पीढ़ियों के बाद कोशिकाओं की संख्या = \\(N_0 \\times 2^n\\)।<br>• द्विविभाजन <b>अमीबा</b> और <b>पैरामीशियम</b> में भी होता है; <b>प्लाज़्मोडियम</b> में बहुविभाजन होता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000073830","section":"GK","topic":"Chemistry: Chemical Reactions","question":{"en":"In a hydrogen–oxygen fuel cell, why are porous electrodes coated or impregnated with a catalyst primarily used? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"हाइड्रोजन–ऑक्सीजन ईंधन सेल में उत्प्रेरक से लेपित या संसेचित सरंध्र इलेक्ट्रोड मुख्य रूप से क्यों उपयोग किए जाते हैं? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To provide large surface area and enhance reaction kinetics","hi":"बड़ा सतही क्षेत्रफल प्रदान करने और अभिक्रिया की गति बढ़ाने के लिए"},"2":{"en":"To increase mechanical strength of the electrodes","hi":"इलेक्ट्रोडों की यांत्रिक शक्ति बढ़ाने के लिए"},"3":{"en":"To store hydrogen and oxygen inside the electrode permanently","hi":"इलेक्ट्रोड के भीतर हाइड्रोजन और ऑक्सीजन को स्थायी रूप से संग्रहीत करने के लिए"},"4":{"en":"To prevent formation of water during the reaction","hi":"अभिक्रिया के दौरान जल के निर्माण को रोकने के लिए"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – To provide large surface area and enhance reaction kinetics</b><br>Porous carbon electrodes with finely divided <b>platinum/palladium</b> catalyst <b><u>provide a large surface area and speed up the electrode reactions</u></b>, so H₂ and O₂ react efficiently to produce electricity.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Overall reaction: \\(2H_2 + O_2 \\rightarrow 2H_2O\\); the only by-product is <b>water</b>, so it is pollution-free.<br>• Electrolyte used: concentrated aqueous <b>KOH</b>.<br>• Fuel cells were used in the <b>Apollo space programme</b>; efficiency is about <b>70%</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – बड़ा सतही क्षेत्रफल प्रदान करने और अभिक्रिया की गति बढ़ाने के लिए</b><br>बारीक विभाजित <b>प्लैटिनम/पैलेडियम</b> उत्प्रेरक वाले सरंध्र कार्बन इलेक्ट्रोड <b><u>बड़ा सतही क्षेत्रफल प्रदान करते हैं और इलेक्ट्रोड अभिक्रियाओं की गति बढ़ाते हैं</u></b>, जिससे H₂ और O₂ कुशलता से अभिक्रिया करके विद्युत उत्पन्न करते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• समग्र अभिक्रिया: \\(2H_2 + O_2 \\rightarrow 2H_2O\\); एकमात्र उपोत्पाद <b>जल</b> है, अतः यह प्रदूषण-मुक्त है।<br>• प्रयुक्त विद्युत-अपघट्य: सांद्र जलीय <b>KOH</b>।<br>• ईंधन सेलों का उपयोग <b>अपोलो अंतरिक्ष कार्यक्रम</b> में हुआ; दक्षता लगभग <b>70%</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000073831","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A right prism has a triangular base with sides 3 cm, 4 cm, and 5 cm. If the height of the prism is 6 cm, what is its volume? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक लंब प्रिज़्म का आधार त्रिभुज है जिसकी भुजाएँ 3 cm, 4 cm और 5 cm हैं। यदि प्रिज़्म की ऊँचाई 6 cm है, तो उसका आयतन क्या है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"36 cm³"},"2":{"en":"48 cm³"},"3":{"en":"54 cm³"},"4":{"en":"60 cm³"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The base is a right triangle (3, 4, 5), so area \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 3 \\times 4 = 6\\) cm²<br>Volume \\(= \\) base area \\(\\times\\) height \\(= 6 \\times 6\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{36\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 36 cm³.</b>","hi":"आधार समकोण त्रिभुज (3, 4, 5) है, अतः क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 3 \\times 4 = 6\\) cm²<br>आयतन \\(= \\) आधार क्षेत्रफल \\(\\times\\) ऊँचाई \\(= 6 \\times 6\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{36\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 36 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000073832","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Simplify: √900 + √0.0625 − √16.81. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सरलीकृत कीजिए: √900 + √0.0625 − √16.81। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"14.37"},"2":{"en":"19.65"},"3":{"en":"23.06"},"4":{"en":"26.15"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{900} = 30\\), \\(\\sqrt{0.0625} = 0.25\\), \\(\\sqrt{16.81} = 4.1\\)<br>\\(= 30 + 0.25 - 4.1\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{26.15}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 26.15.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{900} = 30\\), \\(\\sqrt{0.0625} = 0.25\\), \\(\\sqrt{16.81} = 4.1\\)<br>\\(= 30 + 0.25 - 4.1\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{26.15}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 26.15 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000073833","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In △ABC, the medians AD, BE, and CF intersect at the centroid G. If the length of median AD is 12 cm, what is the length of the segment GD? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"△ABC में, माध्यिकाएँ AD, BE और CF केंद्रक G पर प्रतिच्छेद करती हैं। यदि माध्यिका AD की लंबाई 12 cm है, तो खंड GD की लंबाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 cm"},"2":{"en":"2.5 cm"},"3":{"en":"4 cm"},"4":{"en":"6.1 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The centroid divides each median in the ratio 2 : 1 from the vertex<br>\\(GD = \\frac{1}{3} \\times AD = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 12\\)<br>\\(GD = \\boxed{4\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 4 cm.</b>","hi":"केंद्रक प्रत्येक माध्यिका को शीर्ष से 2 : 1 के अनुपात में विभाजित करता है<br>\\(GD = \\frac{1}{3} \\times AD = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 12\\)<br>\\(GD = \\boxed{4\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 4 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000073834","section":"MATH","topic":"LCM and HCF","question":{"en":"Find the smallest perfect square divisible by 10, 12, 15, and 18. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"10, 12, 15 और 18 से विभाज्य सबसे छोटा पूर्ण वर्ग ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"600"},"2":{"en":"900"},"3":{"en":"500"},"4":{"en":"400"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\text{LCM}(10, 12, 15, 18) = 180 = 2^2 \\times 3^2 \\times 5\\)<br>To make every exponent even, multiply by 5<br>Required square \\(= 180 \\times 5 = \\boxed{900}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 900.</b>","hi":"\\(\\text{LCM}(10, 12, 15, 18) = 180 = 2^2 \\times 3^2 \\times 5\\)<br>सभी घातों को सम बनाने के लिए 5 से गुणा करें<br>अभीष्ट वर्ग \\(= 180 \\times 5 = \\boxed{900}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 900 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000073835","section":"MATH","topic":"Partnership","question":{"en":"Two individuals, A and B, share their profit in a ratio of 3:2. A third person, C, is given a one-fourth share of the profit and contributes ₹12,000 as his capital to the business. What is the capital contribution of B? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो व्यक्ति A और B अपना लाभ 3:2 के अनुपात में बाँटते हैं। एक तीसरे व्यक्ति C को लाभ का एक-चौथाई हिस्सा दिया जाता है और वह व्यवसाय में पूँजी के रूप में ₹12,000 का योगदान देता है। B का पूँजी योगदान क्या है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹18,000"},"2":{"en":"₹14,400"},"3":{"en":"₹21,600"},"4":{"en":"₹15,000"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"C takes \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) of the profit, so A and B share the remaining \\(\\frac{3}{4}\\) in 3 : 2<br>A : B : C \\(= \\frac{3}{4} \\times \\frac{3}{5} : \\frac{3}{4} \\times \\frac{2}{5} : \\frac{1}{4} = 9 : 6 : 5\\)<br>C's 5 parts \\(= 12{,}000 \\Rightarrow 1\\) part \\(= 2400\\)<br>B ₹\\(= 6 \\times 2400 = \\boxed{14{,}400}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹14,400.</b>","hi":"C लाभ का \\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) लेता है, अतः A और B शेष \\(\\frac{3}{4}\\) को 3 : 2 में बाँटते हैं<br>A : B : C \\(= \\frac{3}{4} \\times \\frac{3}{5} : \\frac{3}{4} \\times \\frac{2}{5} : \\frac{1}{4} = 9 : 6 : 5\\)<br>C के 5 भाग \\(= 12{,}000 \\Rightarrow 1\\) भाग \\(= 2400\\)<br>B ₹\\(= 6 \\times 2400 = \\boxed{14{,}400}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹14,400 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000073836","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"The amount of a sum at the end of the 1st year is ₹4,500 and at the end of the 2nd year is ₹4,950. Find its approximate principal. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी धनराशि का पहले वर्ष के अंत में मिश्रधन ₹4,500 और दूसरे वर्ष के अंत में ₹4,950 है। उसका अनुमानित मूलधन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹3981"},"2":{"en":"₹4001"},"3":{"en":"₹3801"},"4":{"en":"₹4091"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Interest for the 2nd year \\(= 4950 - 4500 = 450\\)<br>Rate \\(= \\frac{450}{4500} \\times 100 = 10\\%\\)<br>₹\\(P = \\frac{4500}{1.1} = 4090.9 \\approx \\boxed{4091}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ₹4091.</b>","hi":"दूसरे वर्ष का ब्याज \\(= 4950 - 4500 = 450\\)<br>दर \\(= \\frac{450}{4500} \\times 100 = 10\\%\\)<br>₹\\(P = \\frac{4500}{1.1} = 4090.9 \\approx \\boxed{4091}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ₹4091 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000073837","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A regular hexagon and a square having the same perimeter. If the area of the square is 196 cm², find the exact area of the hexagon. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक सम षट्भुज और एक वर्ग का परिमाप समान है। यदि वर्ग का क्षेत्रफल 196 cm² है, तो षट्भुज का सटीक क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{203\\sqrt{7}}{3}\\) cm²"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{323\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\) cm²"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{210\\sqrt{3}}{9}\\) cm²"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{392\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\) cm²"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Square: side \\(= \\sqrt{196} = 14\\), perimeter \\(= 56\\)<br>Hexagon side \\(= \\frac{56}{6} = \\frac{28}{3}\\)<br>Area \\(= \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times \\left(\\frac{28}{3}\\right)^2 = \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times \\frac{784}{9}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{392\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(\\frac{392\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\) cm².</b>","hi":"वर्ग: भुजा \\(= \\sqrt{196} = 14\\), परिमाप \\(= 56\\)<br>षट्भुज की भुजा \\(= \\frac{56}{6} = \\frac{28}{3}\\)<br>क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times \\left(\\frac{28}{3}\\right)^2 = \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times \\frac{784}{9}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{392\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(\\frac{392\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\) cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000073838","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A circle has a radius of 7 cm, and a square is drawn around it such that the circle touches all four sides. Find the area of the square. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक वृत्त की त्रिज्या 7 cm है और उसके चारों ओर एक वर्ग इस प्रकार बनाया गया है कि वृत्त चारों भुजाओं को स्पर्श करता है। वर्ग का क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"196 cm²"},"2":{"en":"126 cm²"},"3":{"en":"183 cm²"},"4":{"en":"191 cm²"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The side of the square equals the diameter of the incircle<br>\\(a = 2 \\times 7 = 14\\) cm<br>Area \\(= 14^2 = \\boxed{196\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 196 cm².</b>","hi":"वर्ग की भुजा अंतर्वृत्त के व्यास के बराबर होती है<br>\\(a = 2 \\times 7 = 14\\) cm<br>क्षेत्रफल \\(= 14^2 = \\boxed{196\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 196 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000073839","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"If the area of a quadrant of a circle is \\(\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\) m², find the radius (in meters). [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि किसी वृत्त के चतुर्थांश का क्षेत्रफल \\(\\frac{\\pi}{16}\\) m² है, तो त्रिज्या (मीटर में) ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\) m"},"2":{"en":"1 m"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) m"},"4":{"en":"2 m"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\pi r^2 = \\frac{\\pi}{16}\\)<br>\\(r^2 = \\frac{1}{4}\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) m.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{1}{4}\\pi r^2 = \\frac{\\pi}{16}\\)<br>\\(r^2 = \\frac{1}{4}\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000073840","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A cone has a volume of 192π cm³ and a height of 12 cm. Find the radius of its base. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक शंकु का आयतन 192π cm³ और ऊँचाई 12 cm है। उसके आधार की त्रिज्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(4\\sqrt{3}\\) cm"},"2":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{3}\\) cm"},"3":{"en":"\\(5\\sqrt{3}\\) cm"},"4":{"en":"\\(6\\sqrt{3}\\) cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 \\times 12 = 192\\pi\\)<br>\\(4r^2 = 192 \\Rightarrow r^2 = 48\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{4\\sqrt{3}\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(4\\sqrt{3}\\) cm.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 \\times 12 = 192\\pi\\)<br>\\(4r^2 = 192 \\Rightarrow r^2 = 48\\)<br>\\(r = \\boxed{4\\sqrt{3}\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(4\\sqrt{3}\\) cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000073841","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"A shopkeeper makes 15% profit by selling a book at a certain price. If he charges ₹12 more, he would gain 20%. What was the original selling price of the book? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक दुकानदार एक पुस्तक को किसी मूल्य पर बेचकर 15% लाभ कमाता है। यदि वह ₹12 अधिक लेता, तो उसे 20% लाभ होता। पुस्तक का मूल विक्रय मूल्य क्या था? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹296"},"2":{"en":"₹250"},"3":{"en":"₹280"},"4":{"en":"₹276"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Difference of profit \\(= 20\\% - 15\\% = 5\\%\\) of CP \\(= 12\\)<br>CP \\(= \\frac{12}{0.05} = 240\\)<br>Original SP ₹\\(= 240 \\times 1.15 = \\boxed{276}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ₹276.</b>","hi":"लाभ का अंतर \\(= 20\\% - 15\\% = 5\\%\\) (क्रय मूल्य का) \\(= 12\\)<br>क्रय मूल्य \\(= \\frac{12}{0.05} = 240\\)<br>मूल विक्रय मूल्य ₹\\(= 240 \\times 1.15 = \\boxed{276}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ₹276 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000073842","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"A shopkeeper marks up his goods by 60%. He sells 25% of the stock at the marked price, 50% of the stock at a 20% discount on the marked price, and the remaining stock at a 50% discount on the marked price. Find his overall profit percentage. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक दुकानदार अपने माल पर 60% अधिक अंकन करता है। वह 25% स्टॉक अंकित मूल्य पर, 50% स्टॉक अंकित मूल्य पर 20% छूट के साथ और शेष स्टॉक अंकित मूल्य पर 50% छूट के साथ बेचता है। उसका कुल लाभ प्रतिशत ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"28%"},"2":{"en":"24%"},"3":{"en":"32%"},"4":{"en":"45%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let CP \\(= 100\\), MP \\(= 160\\)<br>Revenue \\(= 0.25(160) + 0.5(0.8 \\times 160) + 0.25(0.5 \\times 160) = 40 + 64 + 20 = 124\\)<br>Profit \\(= \\boxed{24\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 24%.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए क्रय मूल्य \\(= 100\\), अंकित मूल्य \\(= 160\\)<br>आय \\(= 0.25(160) + 0.5(0.8 \\times 160) + 0.25(0.5 \\times 160) = 40 + 64 + 20 = 124\\)<br>लाभ \\(= \\boxed{24\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 24% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000073843","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"The angles of elevation of the top of a tower from two points on the same line are 45° and 60°. The points are 20 m apart. Find the approximate height of the tower. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक ही रेखा पर स्थित दो बिंदुओं से मीनार के शिखर के उन्नयन कोण 45° और 60° हैं। बिंदुओं के बीच की दूरी 20 m है। मीनार की अनुमानित ऊँचाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"57.3 m"},"2":{"en":"43.3 m"},"3":{"en":"51.3 m"},"4":{"en":"47.3 m"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{h}{\\tan 45°} - \\frac{h}{\\tan 60°} = 20\\)<br>\\(h\\left(1 - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right) = 20 \\Rightarrow h = \\frac{20}{0.4226}\\)<br>\\(h \\approx \\boxed{47.3\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 47.3 m.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{h}{\\tan 45°} - \\frac{h}{\\tan 60°} = 20\\)<br>\\(h\\left(1 - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right) = 20 \\Rightarrow h = \\frac{20}{0.4226}\\)<br>\\(h \\approx \\boxed{47.3\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 47.3 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000073844","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"The measure of supplement of ∠p is 60° more than four times the measure of complement of ∠p. Find the sum in degree of the supplement and complement of ∠p. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"∠p के संपूरक का माप ∠p के पूरक के माप के चार गुने से 60° अधिक है। ∠p के संपूरक और पूरक का योग (डिग्री में) ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"110°"},"2":{"en":"170°"},"3":{"en":"180°"},"4":{"en":"140°"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\((180° - p) = 60° + 4(90° - p)\\)<br>\\(180° - p = 60° + 360° - 4p \\Rightarrow 3p = 240° \\Rightarrow p = 80°\\)<br>Supplement \\(= 100°\\), complement \\(= 10°\\)<br>Sum \\(= \\boxed{110°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 110°.</b>","hi":"\\((180° - p) = 60° + 4(90° - p)\\)<br>\\(180° - p = 60° + 360° - 4p \\Rightarrow 3p = 240° \\Rightarrow p = 80°\\)<br>संपूरक \\(= 100°\\), पूरक \\(= 10°\\)<br>योग \\(= \\boxed{110°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 110° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000073845","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sin A - \\cos A = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\) and angle A lies in the first quadrant, find the value of sin A + cos A. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(\\sin A - \\cos A = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\) है और कोण A प्रथम चतुर्थांश में है, तो sin A + cos A का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\)"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\((\\sin A + \\cos A)^2 + (\\sin A - \\cos A)^2 = 2\\)<br>\\((\\sin A + \\cos A)^2 = 2 - \\frac{2}{4} = \\frac{3}{2}\\)<br>\\(\\sin A + \\cos A = \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2} = \\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\).</b>","hi":"\\((\\sin A + \\cos A)^2 + (\\sin A - \\cos A)^2 = 2\\)<br>\\((\\sin A + \\cos A)^2 = 2 - \\frac{2}{4} = \\frac{3}{2}\\)<br>\\(\\sin A + \\cos A = \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2} = \\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000073846","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"What is the value of \\(\\frac{5\\csc^2 30° - 3\\cot^2 30° + 16\\cos^4 45°}{2\\sqrt{3}\\tan 60° + 4\\sin^2 60°}\\)? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"\\(\\frac{5\\csc^2 30° - 3\\cot^2 30° + 16\\cos^4 45°}{2\\sqrt{3}\\tan 60° + 4\\sin^2 60°}\\) का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{5}{3}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{2}\\)"},"4":{"en":"0"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\csc 30° = 2\\), \\(\\cot 30° = \\sqrt{3}\\), \\(\\cos 45° = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\), \\(\\tan 60° = \\sqrt{3}\\), \\(\\sin 60° = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\)<br>Numerator \\(= 5(4) - 3(3) + 16\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right) = 20 - 9 + 4 = 15\\)<br>Denominator \\(= 2\\sqrt{3}(\\sqrt{3}) + 4\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right) = 6 + 3 = 9\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{15}{9} = \\boxed{\\frac{5}{3}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(\\frac{5}{3}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\csc 30° = 2\\), \\(\\cot 30° = \\sqrt{3}\\), \\(\\cos 45° = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\), \\(\\tan 60° = \\sqrt{3}\\), \\(\\sin 60° = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\)<br>अंश \\(= 5(4) - 3(3) + 16\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right) = 20 - 9 + 4 = 15\\)<br>हर \\(= 2\\sqrt{3}(\\sqrt{3}) + 4\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right) = 6 + 3 = 9\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{15}{9} = \\boxed{\\frac{5}{3}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(\\frac{5}{3}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000073847","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"Three solid metallic spheres of radii 4 cm, 3 cm, and 5 cm are melted to form a single large sphere. What is the radius of the new sphere? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"4 cm, 3 cm और 5 cm त्रिज्या वाले तीन ठोस धात्विक गोले पिघलाकर एक बड़ा गोला बनाया जाता है। नए गोले की त्रिज्या क्या है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3 cm"},"2":{"en":"6 cm"},"3":{"en":"8 cm"},"4":{"en":"9 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Volume is conserved: \\(R^3 = 4^3 + 3^3 + 5^3\\)<br>\\(= 64 + 27 + 125 = 216\\)<br>\\(R = \\boxed{6\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 6 cm.</b>","hi":"आयतन संरक्षित रहता है: \\(R^3 = 4^3 + 3^3 + 5^3\\)<br>\\(= 64 + 27 + 125 = 216\\)<br>\\(R = \\boxed{6\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 6 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000073848","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Triangles XYZ and PQR are similar. In △XYZ, the side lengths are XY = 10 cm, YZ = 15 cm, and ZX = 20 cm. If the ratio of the areas of △XYZ and △PQR is 25: 36, what is the length of side QR in △PQR? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"त्रिभुज XYZ और PQR समरूप हैं। △XYZ में भुजाओं की लंबाइयाँ XY = 10 cm, YZ = 15 cm और ZX = 20 cm हैं। यदि △XYZ और △PQR के क्षेत्रफलों का अनुपात 25:36 है, तो △PQR में भुजा QR की लंबाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12 cm"},"2":{"en":"14 cm"},"3":{"en":"18 cm"},"4":{"en":"20 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Area ratio \\(= 25 : 36\\), so side ratio \\(= 5 : 6\\)<br>QR corresponds to YZ \\(= 15\\) cm<br>\\(QR = 15 \\times \\frac{6}{5} = \\boxed{18\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 18 cm.</b>","hi":"क्षेत्रफल अनुपात \\(= 25 : 36\\), अतः भुजा अनुपात \\(= 5 : 6\\)<br>QR, YZ \\(= 15\\) cm के संगत है<br>\\(QR = 15 \\times \\frac{6}{5} = \\boxed{18\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 18 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000073849","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"A cooperative housing society borrowed ₹4,50,000 to repair its buildings. The society paid back ₹6,12,000 after 9 years. Find the rate of simple interest and determine how much interest was paid every year. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक सहकारी आवास समिति ने अपने भवनों की मरम्मत के लिए ₹4,50,000 उधार लिए। समिति ने 9 वर्षों बाद ₹6,12,000 वापस चुकाए। साधारण ब्याज की दर ज्ञात कीजिए और प्रति वर्ष दिया गया ब्याज भी बताइए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rate of Simple Interest = 5% per annum<br>Interest paid every year = ₹21,000","hi":"साधारण ब्याज की दर = 5% प्रति वर्ष<br>प्रति वर्ष दिया गया ब्याज = ₹21,000"},"2":{"en":"Rate of Simple Interest = 2% per annum<br>Interest paid every year = ₹19,000","hi":"साधारण ब्याज की दर = 2% प्रति वर्ष<br>प्रति वर्ष दिया गया ब्याज = ₹19,000"},"3":{"en":"Rate of Simple Interest = 4% per annum<br>Interest paid every year = ₹18,000","hi":"साधारण ब्याज की दर = 4% प्रति वर्ष<br>प्रति वर्ष दिया गया ब्याज = ₹18,000"},"4":{"en":"Rate of Simple Interest = 3% per annum<br>Interest paid every year = ₹17,000","hi":"साधारण ब्याज की दर = 3% प्रति वर्ष<br>प्रति वर्ष दिया गया ब्याज = ₹17,000"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Total interest \\(= 6{,}12{,}000 - 4{,}50{,}000 = 1{,}62{,}000\\)<br>Per year \\(= \\frac{1{,}62{,}000}{9} = 18{,}000\\)<br>Rate \\(= \\frac{18{,}000}{4{,}50{,}000} \\times 100 = 4\\%\\)<br>₹\\(= \\boxed{\\text{Rate } 4\\% \\text{ per annum, interest } 18{,}000 \\text{ per year}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Rate of Simple Interest = 4% per annum<br>Interest paid every year = ₹18,000.</b>","hi":"कुल ब्याज \\(= 6{,}12{,}000 - 4{,}50{,}000 = 1{,}62{,}000\\)<br>प्रति वर्ष \\(= \\frac{1{,}62{,}000}{9} = 18{,}000\\)<br>दर \\(= \\frac{18{,}000}{4{,}50{,}000} \\times 100 = 4\\%\\)<br>₹\\(= \\boxed{\\text{दर } 4\\% \\text{ प्रति वर्ष, ब्याज } 18{,}000 \\text{ प्रति वर्ष}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): साधारण ब्याज की दर = 4% प्रति वर्ष<br>प्रति वर्ष दिया गया ब्याज = ₹18,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000073850","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"An expert potter can craft a batch of pottery in 24 hours, while his apprentice can do the same in 40 hours. They receive a large high-profile order of a batch from the owner of a hotel and decide to work on it together. However, a strict quality inspector is sent by the hotel owner at the exact end of every 4-hour joint shift. The inspector rejects exactly 20% of the pottery completed during those specific 4-hour shifts due to minor imperfections. Any final remaining items needed after the last shift are crafted under direct guidance with 0% defects. How many total hours will it take them to complete the order successfully? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक कुशल कुम्हार 24 घंटे में मिट्टी के बर्तनों का एक बैच बना सकता है, जबकि उसका शिष्य यही काम 40 घंटे में कर सकता है। उन्हें एक होटल के मालिक से बड़ा ऑर्डर मिलता है और वे मिलकर काम करने का निर्णय लेते हैं। होटल मालिक हर 4 घंटे की संयुक्त पाली के ठीक अंत में एक कड़ा गुणवत्ता निरीक्षक भेजता है। निरीक्षक उन 4 घंटों में बने बर्तनों का ठीक 20% खराबी के कारण अस्वीकार कर देता है। अंतिम पाली के बाद बचे बर्तन सीधे निगरानी में 0% खराबी के साथ बनाए जाते हैं। ऑर्डर पूरा करने में कुल कितने घंटे लगेंगे? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"18.2 hrs","hi":"18.2 घंटे"},"2":{"en":"17.4 hrs","hi":"17.4 घंटे"},"3":{"en":"16.8 hrs","hi":"16.8 घंटे"},"4":{"en":"15.5 hrs","hi":"15.5 घंटे"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Combined rate \\(= \\frac{1}{24} + \\frac{1}{40} = \\frac{8}{120} = \\frac{1}{15}\\) per hour<br>In one 4-hour shift they do \\(\\frac{4}{15}\\); after 20% rejection \\(= 0.8 \\times \\frac{4}{15} = \\frac{3.2}{15}\\)<br>After 4 shifts (16 hrs): \\(4 \\times \\frac{3.2}{15} = \\frac{12.8}{15} = 0.8533\\)<br>Remaining \\(= 1 - 0.8533 = 0.1467\\), made with 0% defects at \\(\\frac{1}{15}\\) per hour<br>Extra time \\(= 0.1467 \\times 15 = 2.2\\) hrs<br>Total \\(= 16 + 2.2 = \\boxed{18.2\\ \\text{hrs}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 18.2 hrs.</b>","hi":"संयुक्त दर \\(= \\frac{1}{24} + \\frac{1}{40} = \\frac{8}{120} = \\frac{1}{15}\\) प्रति घंटा<br>एक 4 घंटे की पाली में \\(\\frac{4}{15}\\) कार्य; 20% अस्वीकृति के बाद \\(= 0.8 \\times \\frac{4}{15} = \\frac{3.2}{15}\\)<br>4 पालियों (16 घंटे) बाद: \\(4 \\times \\frac{3.2}{15} = \\frac{12.8}{15} = 0.8533\\)<br>शेष \\(= 1 - 0.8533 = 0.1467\\), जो 0% खराबी के साथ \\(\\frac{1}{15}\\) प्रति घंटा की दर से बनेगा<br>अतिरिक्त समय \\(= 0.1467 \\times 15 = 2.2\\) घंटे<br>कुल \\(= 16 + 2.2 = \\boxed{18.2\\ \\text{घंटे}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 18.2 घंटे है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000073851","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A team of linguists is translating the text on an ancient monolith. Linguist A and linguist B working together can translate it in 12 days, linguist B and linguist C working together can do it in 15 days, while A and C working together can do it in 20 days. All three of them work together on the monolith for 6 days. Then, A and B are relocated to another site. How many more days will be required by C to finish the remaining task alone? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भाषाविदों की एक टीम एक प्राचीन शिलालेख का पाठ अनुवाद कर रही है। भाषाविद् A और B मिलकर इसे 12 दिनों में, B और C मिलकर 15 दिनों में तथा A और C मिलकर 20 दिनों में अनुवाद कर सकते हैं। तीनों मिलकर 6 दिन कार्य करते हैं। फिर A और B को दूसरे स्थल पर भेज दिया जाता है। शेष कार्य C अकेले पूरा करने में कितने और दिन लेगा? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20 days","hi":"20 दिन"},"2":{"en":"22 days","hi":"22 दिन"},"3":{"en":"24 days","hi":"24 दिन"},"4":{"en":"25 days","hi":"25 दिन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(2(A + B + C) = \\frac{1}{12} + \\frac{1}{15} + \\frac{1}{20} = \\frac{5 + 4 + 3}{60} = \\frac{1}{5}\\)<br>So \\(A + B + C = \\frac{1}{10}\\) and \\(C = \\frac{1}{10} - \\frac{1}{12} = \\frac{1}{60}\\)<br>6 days' work \\(= \\frac{6}{10} = 0.6\\), remaining \\(= 0.4\\)<br>C alone \\(= 0.4 \\times 60 = \\boxed{24\\ \\text{days}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 24 days.</b>","hi":"\\(2(A + B + C) = \\frac{1}{12} + \\frac{1}{15} + \\frac{1}{20} = \\frac{5 + 4 + 3}{60} = \\frac{1}{5}\\)<br>अतः \\(A + B + C = \\frac{1}{10}\\) और \\(C = \\frac{1}{10} - \\frac{1}{12} = \\frac{1}{60}\\)<br>6 दिन का कार्य \\(= \\frac{6}{10} = 0.6\\), शेष \\(= 0.4\\)<br>C अकेले \\(= 0.4 \\times 60 = \\boxed{24\\ \\text{दिन}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 24 दिन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000073852","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Evaluate: \\(\\frac{\\sin 35°}{\\cos 55°}\\) [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मान ज्ञात कीजिए: \\(\\frac{\\sin 35°}{\\cos 55°}\\) [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"0"},"3":{"en":"−1"},"4":{"en":"2"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\cos 55° = \\cos(90° - 35°) = \\sin 35°\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{\\sin 35°}{\\sin 35°}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1.</b>","hi":"\\(\\cos 55° = \\cos(90° - 35°) = \\sin 35°\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{\\sin 35°}{\\sin 35°}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000073853","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Evaluate the following numerical expression using an appropriate algebraic identity:<br>\\(\\frac{5.37 \\times 5.37 - 4.63 \\times 4.63}{0.74}\\) [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उपयुक्त बीजगणितीय सर्वसमिका का उपयोग करके निम्नलिखित संख्यात्मक व्यंजक का मान ज्ञात कीजिए:<br>\\(\\frac{5.37 \\times 5.37 - 4.63 \\times 4.63}{0.74}\\) [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"7.3"},"3":{"en":"4.6"},"4":{"en":"10"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\) with \\(a = 5.37\\), \\(b = 4.63\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{(5.37 - 4.63)(5.37 + 4.63)}{0.74} = \\frac{0.74 \\times 10}{0.74}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{10}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 10.</b>","hi":"\\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\), जहाँ \\(a = 5.37\\), \\(b = 4.63\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{(5.37 - 4.63)(5.37 + 4.63)}{0.74} = \\frac{0.74 \\times 10}{0.74}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{10}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 10 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000073854","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If a + b = 18 and ab = 46, compute a³ + b³. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि a + b = 18 और ab = 46 है, तो a³ + b³ का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2484"},"2":{"en":"3348"},"3":{"en":"4328"},"4":{"en":"5832"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(a^3 + b^3 = (a + b)^3 - 3ab(a + b)\\)<br>\\(= 18^3 - 3(46)(18) = 5832 - 2484\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3348}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 3348.</b>","hi":"\\(a^3 + b^3 = (a + b)^3 - 3ab(a + b)\\)<br>\\(= 18^3 - 3(46)(18) = 5832 - 2484\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3348}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 3348 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000073855","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Simplify the following expression completely:<br>\\(\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5} + \\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5} - \\sqrt{2}}\\) [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित व्यंजक को पूर्णतः सरल कीजिए:<br>\\(\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5} + \\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5} - \\sqrt{2}}\\) [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{5\\sqrt{5} + \\sqrt{2}}{3}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\sqrt{5} - 5\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{5\\sqrt{5} - \\sqrt{2}}{3}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{5}}\\)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Rationalise each term: \\(\\frac{3(\\sqrt{5} - \\sqrt{2})}{3} + \\frac{2(\\sqrt{5} + \\sqrt{2})}{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{3\\sqrt{5} - 3\\sqrt{2} + 2\\sqrt{5} + 2\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{5\\sqrt{5} - \\sqrt{2}}{3}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(\\frac{5\\sqrt{5} - \\sqrt{2}}{3}\\).</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद का परिमेयकरण: \\(\\frac{3(\\sqrt{5} - \\sqrt{2})}{3} + \\frac{2(\\sqrt{5} + \\sqrt{2})}{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{3\\sqrt{5} - 3\\sqrt{2} + 2\\sqrt{5} + 2\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{5\\sqrt{5} - \\sqrt{2}}{3}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(\\frac{5\\sqrt{5} - \\sqrt{2}}{3}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000073856","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Choose the accurate direct speech version of the following sentence.<br><br>She asked me to tell her the location of the guest house. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"She said, \"I was wondering if you could possibly tell me the location of the guest house?\""},"2":{"en":"She asked, “Could you tell me the location of the guest house?”"},"3":{"en":"She said, \"Tell me the location of the guest house.\""},"4":{"en":"She asked, \"Could you possibly tell me the location of the guest house?\""}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'asked + object + to + V1' reports an imperative; in direct speech it becomes 'said, \"V1 …\"'; 'her' → 'me'.</b><br>Direct: She said, \"<b>Tell me</b> the location of the guest house.\"<br>Option 1 – turns the order into a long statement-question<br>Option 2 – turns the order into a polite question; 'asked' kept as the reporting verb<br>Option 4 – a question form is not the direct form of 'asked … to'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): She said, \"Tell me the location of the guest house.\".</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000073857","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br><br>The recent advancements in space exploration<br>P. and paving the way for future Mars colonization<br>Q. unlocking new possibilities for interplanetary travel,<br>R. have been driven by international collaborations,<br>S. focused on developing sustainable lunar habitats [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PSQR"},"2":{"en":"RQSP"},"3":{"en":"SRPQ"},"4":{"en":"QPSR"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RQSP</b><br><b>R</b> 'have been driven by international collaborations,' gives the verb for the subject.<br><b>Q</b> 'unlocking new possibilities for interplanetary travel,' shows the first result.<br><b>S</b> 'focused on developing sustainable lunar habitats' describes the work.<br><b>P</b> 'and paving the way for future Mars colonization' adds the last result with 'and'.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): RQSP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000073858","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct phrase for the word highlighted in bold.<br><br>\"He expects his subordinates to be always <b>at his beck and call</b>\"? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To be constantly available to obey orders"},"2":{"en":"To challenge authority frequently"},"3":{"en":"To work only when convenient"},"4":{"en":"To ignore requests deliberately"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>At someone's beck and call (हर समय हुक्म बजाने को तैयार) = always ready to obey someone's orders.</b><br>Example: The minister expects his staff to be at his beck and call.<br>Challenge authority (अधिकार को चुनौती देना) – opposite<br>Work only when convenient (सुविधा से काम करना) – opposite<br>Ignore requests (अनुरोध अनदेखा करना) – opposite<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): To be constantly available to obey orders.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000073859","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Phrasal Verbs","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with an appropriate phrasal verb.<br><br>Despite initial enthusiasm, investors began to ______ when the project’s viability was questioned. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"backwash"},"2":{"en":"backpedal"},"3":{"en":"backlash"},"4":{"en":"backburn"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Backpedal (पीछे हटना) = to withdraw from an earlier position or commitment.</b><br>Investors who were enthusiastic began to withdraw their support when doubts arose.<br>Correct sentence: …investors began to <b>backpedal</b> when the project's viability was questioned.<br><b>Backwash (उलटी लहर)</b> = water pushed back; an after-effect<br><b>Backlash (तीव्र विरोध)</b> = a strong negative reaction – a noun<br><b>Backburn (प्रति-आग)</b> = a controlled fire to check a forest fire<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): backpedal.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000073860","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Identify the error in the sentence.<br><br>She’s reading an Times of India editorial. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"India"},"2":{"en":"an"},"3":{"en":"editorial"},"4":{"en":"reading"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'an' is used before a vowel sound; 'Times' begins with the consonant sound /t/.</b><br>The article must be 'a' (or 'the' before the name of the newspaper).<br>Correct sentence: She's reading <b>a</b> Times of India editorial.<br>'reading', 'India' and 'editorial' are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): an.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000073861","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?</b><br><br>1. However, rising ocean temperatures and acidification are causing coral bleaching, threatening reef survival.<br>2. Corals have a symbiotic relationship with algae, which provide them with nutrients and vibrant colors.<br>3. When stressed by environmental changes, corals expel the algae, leading to their pale, bleached appearance.<br>4. Coral reefs are among the most biodiverse ecosystems, providing habitat for thousands of marine species.<br>5. Scientists are exploring conservation strategies, including artificial reefs and selective breeding of heat-resistant coral species. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-3-1-4-5"},"2":{"en":"3-1-4-2-5"},"3":{"en":"4-2-1-3-5"},"4":{"en":"5-4-1-3-2"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 4-2-1-3-5</b><br><b>4</b> introduces coral reefs and their importance.<br><b>2</b> explains their link with algae.<br><b>1</b> 'However' brings in the threat of coral bleaching.<br><b>3</b> explains how bleaching happens.<br><b>5</b> concludes with conservation efforts.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 4-2-1-3-5.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000073862","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Improve the sentence by choosing the correct degree of comparison that replaces the word highlighted in bold.<br><br>This road is <b>narrow</b> than the one we took yesterday. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"more narrower"},"2":{"en":"narrower"},"3":{"en":"most narrow"},"4":{"en":"narrowest"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'than' needs the comparative degree; 'narrow' takes '-er'.</b><br>Correct sentence: This road is <b>narrower</b> than the one we took yesterday.<br>more narrower – double comparative<br>most narrow – superlative cannot be used with 'than'<br>narrowest – superlative cannot be used with 'than'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): narrower.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000073863","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word<b>. Zealous</b> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Apathetic"},"2":{"en":"Ardent"},"3":{"en":"Fervent"},"4":{"en":"Eager"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Zealous (उत्साही, जोशीला) = full of great energy or enthusiasm.</b><br><b>Apathetic (उदासीन)</b> = showing no interest or enthusiasm ✔<br><b>Ardent (उत्साही)</b> – synonym<br><b>Fervent (जोशीला)</b> – synonym<br><b>Eager (उत्सुक)</b> – synonym<br>More antonyms: indifferent, unenthusiastic, half-hearted.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Apathetic.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000073864","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom:<br><b>Give someone the slip</b> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To insult someone subtly"},"2":{"en":"To evade or escape from someone unnoticed"},"3":{"en":"To forgive after insult"},"4":{"en":"To follow and copy someone"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Give someone the slip (चकमा देना) = to escape from someone who is following or watching you.</b><br>Example: The thief gave the police the slip in the crowded market.<br>Insult subtly (सूक्ष्म अपमान करना) – unrelated<br>Forgive after insult (अपमान के बाद क्षमा करना) – unrelated<br>Follow and copy (पीछा करना/नकल करना) – opposite of escaping<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): To evade or escape from someone unnoticed.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000073865","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Spot the <b>correct spelling</b> of a word meaning \"gold or silver in bulk form\". [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Bullian"},"2":{"en":"Bullon"},"3":{"en":"Bullion"},"4":{"en":"Bulyon"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Bullion (सोने-चाँदी की सिल्लियाँ) = gold or silver in bulk, as bars, before coining.</b><br>Spelling: bu-<b>ll</b>-<b>ion</b>.<br><b>Bullian</b> – 'a' in place of 'o'<br><b>Bullon</b> – 'i' missing<br><b>Bulyon</b> – single 'l' and 'y' in place of 'li'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Bullion.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000073866","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct <b>one-word substitute</b> for: 'A false name used by an author.' [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Acronym"},"2":{"en":"Pseudonym"},"3":{"en":"Homonym"},"4":{"en":"Patronym"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Pseudonym (छद्म नाम, उपनाम) = a false name used by an author.</b><br><b>Acronym (संक्षिप्ताक्षर)</b> = a word formed from initial letters (e.g. NASA)<br><b>Homonym (समनाम शब्द)</b> = a word with the same spelling or sound but a different meaning<br><b>Patronym (पितृनाम)</b> = a name derived from the father's name<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Pseudonym.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000073867","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct <b>one-word substitute</b> for: 'Excessively idealistic; impractical.' [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Visionary"},"2":{"en":"Pragmatic"},"3":{"en":"Quixotic"},"4":{"en":"Dogmatic"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Quixotic (अव्यावहारिक आदर्शवादी) = extremely idealistic and unrealistic.</b><br><b>Visionary (दूरदर्शी)</b> = having wise ideas about the future – positive, not impractical<br><b>Pragmatic (व्यावहारिक)</b> = practical – opposite<br><b>Dogmatic (हठधर्मी)</b> = insisting one's beliefs are certainly right<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Quixotic.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000073868","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"<b>Select the correct option:</b><br>The document was classified; ___, it could not be circulated publicly. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"therefore"},"2":{"en":"however"},"3":{"en":"nonetheless"},"4":{"en":"otherwise"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: A connector showing result is needed – the second clause follows from the first.</b><br>Because the document was classified, it could not be circulated. 'Therefore (इसलिए)' shows this cause-effect link.<br>Correct sentence: The document was classified; <b>therefore</b>, it could not be circulated publicly.<br><b>however (हालाँकि)</b> – shows contrast<br><b>nonetheless (फिर भी)</b> – shows contrast<br><b>otherwise (अन्यथा)</b> – shows an alternative result<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): therefore.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000073869","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"<b>Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:</b><br>She wore a stunning red silk long scarf (1) that complemented her traditional attire (2) during the award ceremony (3) at the convention centre. (4) [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Order of adjectives – opinion, size/length, age, shape, colour, origin, material, purpose + noun.</b><br>In part (1) 'long' (size) must come before 'red' (colour) and 'silk' (material).<br>Correct sentence: She wore a <b>stunning long red silk scarf</b> that complemented her traditional attire during the award ceremony at the convention centre.<br>Parts (2), (3) and (4) are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): (1).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000073870","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"<b>Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:</b><br>It seems as though the department is reluctant (1)/ not because of the cost implications, (2)/ but because that it might signal (3)/ a policy shift they are not ready to make. (4) [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'because' is itself a conjunction; it is not followed by 'that'.</b><br>Part (3) 'because that it might' must be 'because it might'.<br>Correct sentence: …not because of the cost implications, but <b>because it might</b> signal a policy shift they are not ready to make.<br>Part (1) 'as though' is correct; part (2) 'because of + noun' is correct; part (4) is correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): (3).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000073871","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"<b>Change the following from active to passive:</b><br>They will have been scrutinizing the proposal all afternoon. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The proposal will have scrutinized all afternoon."},"2":{"en":"The proposal will have had been been scrutinized all afternoon."},"3":{"en":"The proposal will have be being scrutinized all afternoon."},"4":{"en":"The proposal will have been being scrutinized all afternoon."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Future perfect continuous (will have been + V-ing) → passive: will have been being + V3.</b><br>'the proposal' becomes the subject; 'by them' is dropped.<br>Passive: The proposal <b>will have been being scrutinized</b> all afternoon.<br>Option 1 – 'been' missing, so the sentence stays active in form<br>Option 2 – 'had been been' is ungrammatical<br>Option 3 – 'have be being' is ungrammatical<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): The proposal will have been being scrutinized all afternoon.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000073872","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"<b>Change the following from active to passive:</b><br>Legal advisors urged the firm to amend the draft immediately. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It was urged that the firm amend the draft immediately."},"2":{"en":"The draft was urged by legal advisors to be amended."},"3":{"en":"The firm was urged by legal advisors to amend the draft immediately."},"4":{"en":"Legal advice was urging amendment of the draft."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Simple past active (V2) → was/were + V3; the person object 'the firm' becomes the subject and the infinitive stays.</b><br>Passive: The firm <b>was urged</b> by legal advisors to amend the draft immediately.<br>Option 1 – drops the agent 'legal advisors'<br>Option 2 – the draft cannot be 'urged'; meaning changes<br>Option 4 – changes the tense and the subject<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): The firm was urged by legal advisors to amend the draft immediately.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000073873","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"<b>A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech.</b><br>She said that she had hardly begun the speech when the microphone failed. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"“Hardly had I begun the speech when the microphone failed,” she said."},"2":{"en":"“I hardly began the speech when the microphone failed,” she said."},"3":{"en":"“The microphone failed as I started speaking,” she said."},"4":{"en":"“The microphone failed just after I began,” she said."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'hardly … when' takes the past perfect (had + V3); in direct speech it is commonly placed first with inversion: Hardly had + subject + V3 … when + V2.</b><br>'she' → 'I'.<br>Direct: “<b>Hardly had I begun</b> the speech when the microphone failed,” she said.<br>Option 2 – 'hardly began' – 'hardly … when' needs the past perfect<br>Options 3 and 4 – rephrase and lose the 'hardly … when' structure<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): “Hardly had I begun the speech when the microphone failed,” she said.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000073874","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"<b>Choose the most appropriate synonym of the underlined word.</b><br><br>The app’s interface is <b><u>concise</u></b> and user-friendly. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lengthy"},"2":{"en":"Detailed"},"3":{"en":"Brief"},"4":{"en":"Confusing"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Concise (संक्षिप्त) = giving information clearly in few words.</b><br><b>Brief (संक्षिप्त)</b> = short ✔<br><b>Lengthy (लंबा)</b> – antonym<br><b>Detailed (विस्तृत)</b> – antonym<br><b>Confusing (भ्रामक)</b> – unrelated<br>More synonyms: succinct, compact, terse.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Brief.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000073875","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>In the following question, the first and last parts of the sentence (1 and 6) are given. The rest of the sentence is split into four parts and named P, Q, R, and S. These four parts are not given in their proper order. Read the sentence and find out which of the four combinations is correct.</b><br><br><b>1. Not only did</b><br>P. the socio-economic conditions<br>Q. but it also highlighted<br>R. the revolution improve<br>S. of the working class<br><b>6. the inherent flaws of the monarchy.</b> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RPSQ"},"2":{"en":"SQRP"},"3":{"en":"RQSP"},"4":{"en":"PQRS"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RPSQ</b><br><b>R</b> 'the revolution improve' follows 'Not only did' (did + subject + V1).<br><b>P</b> 'the socio-economic conditions' is the object.<br><b>S</b> 'of the working class' completes 'conditions of…'.<br><b>Q</b> 'but it also highlighted' completes 'Not only … but also' and joins part 6.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): RPSQ.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000073876","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>Few people truly understand the hidden life of the street. Even when we enter it, we often fail to recognise the unique individuals who belong to it—the wanderers and nomads who have preserved their secrets through generations. We understand even less about the street at night, when it resembles a great house whose doors are locked.<br>Charles Dickens, however, understood the street deeply. He seemed to possess the key to its hidden world. The street lamps were his stars, and the ordinary person on the street was his hero. He could reveal its innermost character and enter its secret passages, lined with houses and roofed with stars.<br>Facts that are merely observed do not remain permanently fixed in memory. To remember a place forever, one must experience it completely and become so deeply absorbed in it that one temporarily forgets oneself as a separate observer.<br>For Dickens, the streets remained deeply romantic because they were associated with the powerful experiences and tragedies of his youth. They were also filled with memories of sunsets that could never return. This emotional connection explains the unusual realism with which he brought the dark and ordinary corners of London to life. In his descriptions, even minor details—a window, a railing or the keyhole of a door—acquire an intense and lifelike vitality. Through his imagination, ordinary objects appear more vivid and real than they normally do.<br><br><br>According to the passage, what distinguished Dickens’s understanding of the street? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"He studied the architectural features of London in great detail."},"2":{"en":"He viewed the street mainly as a setting for dramatic events."},"3":{"en":"He observed street life from a safe and emotional distance."},"4":{"en":"He understood the hidden life and character of the street deeply."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<i>\"Charles Dickens, however, understood the street deeply. He seemed to possess the key to its hidden world… He could reveal its innermost character…\"</i><br>Unlike most people, Dickens knew the street's hidden life and character.<br>Option 1 – architecture is not mentioned<br>Option 2 – the street is not described as just a setting<br>Option 3 – the passage stresses deep emotional involvement, not distance<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): He understood the hidden life and character of the street deeply.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000073877","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>Few people truly understand the hidden life of the street. Even when we enter it, we often fail to recognise the unique individuals who belong to it—the wanderers and nomads who have preserved their secrets through generations. We understand even less about the street at night, when it resembles a great house whose doors are locked.<br>Charles Dickens, however, understood the street deeply. He seemed to possess the key to its hidden world. The street lamps were his stars, and the ordinary person on the street was his hero. He could reveal its innermost character and enter its secret passages, lined with houses and roofed with stars.<br>Facts that are merely observed do not remain permanently fixed in memory. To remember a place forever, one must experience it completely and become so deeply absorbed in it that one temporarily forgets oneself as a separate observer.<br>For Dickens, the streets remained deeply romantic because they were associated with the powerful experiences and tragedies of his youth. They were also filled with memories of sunsets that could never return. This emotional connection explains the unusual realism with which he brought the dark and ordinary corners of London to life. In his descriptions, even minor details—a window, a railing or the keyhole of a door—acquire an intense and lifelike vitality. Through his imagination, ordinary objects appear more vivid and real than they normally do.<br><br><br>What does the comparison of the street at night to “a great house whose doors are locked” suggest? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The street becomes physically inaccessible after sunset."},"2":{"en":"The buildings appear safer and more impressive at night."},"3":{"en":"The hidden life of the street becomes mysterious and difficult to understand."},"4":{"en":"The residents deliberately prevent strangers from entering the street."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<i>\"We understand even less about the street at night, when it resembles a great house whose doors are locked.\"</i><br>Locked doors stand for what we cannot enter or know – the night street's life is hidden and mysterious.<br>Option 1 – literal reading; the street is not closed<br>Option 2 – safety of buildings is not discussed<br>Option 4 – residents keeping people out is not stated<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): The hidden life of the street becomes mysterious and difficult to understand.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000073878","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>Few people truly understand the hidden life of the street. Even when we enter it, we often fail to recognise the unique individuals who belong to it—the wanderers and nomads who have preserved their secrets through generations. We understand even less about the street at night, when it resembles a great house whose doors are locked.<br>Charles Dickens, however, understood the street deeply. He seemed to possess the key to its hidden world. The street lamps were his stars, and the ordinary person on the street was his hero. He could reveal its innermost character and enter its secret passages, lined with houses and roofed with stars.<br>Facts that are merely observed do not remain permanently fixed in memory. To remember a place forever, one must experience it completely and become so deeply absorbed in it that one temporarily forgets oneself as a separate observer.<br>For Dickens, the streets remained deeply romantic because they were associated with the powerful experiences and tragedies of his youth. They were also filled with memories of sunsets that could never return. This emotional connection explains the unusual realism with which he brought the dark and ordinary corners of London to life. In his descriptions, even minor details—a window, a railing or the keyhole of a door—acquire an intense and lifelike vitality. Through his imagination, ordinary objects appear more vivid and real than they normally do.<br><br><br>According to the author, how can a person remember a place permanently? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"By recording all its visible features accurately."},"2":{"en":"By visiting it repeatedly at different times of the day."},"3":{"en":"By comparing it with other familiar surroundings."},"4":{"en":"By becoming completely absorbed in the experience of the place."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<i>\"To remember a place forever, one must experience it completely and become so deeply absorbed in it that one temporarily forgets oneself…\"</i><br>Complete absorption in the experience fixes a place in memory.<br>Option 1 – merely observed facts 'do not remain permanently fixed'<br>Option 2 – repeated visits are not mentioned<br>Option 3 – comparison is not mentioned<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): By becoming completely absorbed in the experience of the place.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000073879","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>Few people truly understand the hidden life of the street. Even when we enter it, we often fail to recognise the unique individuals who belong to it—the wanderers and nomads who have preserved their secrets through generations. We understand even less about the street at night, when it resembles a great house whose doors are locked.<br>Charles Dickens, however, understood the street deeply. He seemed to possess the key to its hidden world. The street lamps were his stars, and the ordinary person on the street was his hero. He could reveal its innermost character and enter its secret passages, lined with houses and roofed with stars.<br>Facts that are merely observed do not remain permanently fixed in memory. To remember a place forever, one must experience it completely and become so deeply absorbed in it that one temporarily forgets oneself as a separate observer.<br>For Dickens, the streets remained deeply romantic because they were associated with the powerful experiences and tragedies of his youth. They were also filled with memories of sunsets that could never return. This emotional connection explains the unusual realism with which he brought the dark and ordinary corners of London to life. In his descriptions, even minor details—a window, a railing or the keyhole of a door—acquire an intense and lifelike vitality. Through his imagination, ordinary objects appear more vivid and real than they normally do.<br><br><br>What is implied by the association of the streets with the powerful experiences and tragedies of Dickens’s youth? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Dickens’s emotional experiences gave the streets lasting personal and romantic significance."},"2":{"en":"The streets were decorated with colours commonly associated with youthful celebrations."},"3":{"en":"Dickens regarded the streets as symbols of political and social decline."},"4":{"en":"The appearance of the streets changed mainly because of the setting sun."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<i>\"For Dickens, the streets remained deeply romantic because they were associated with the powerful experiences and tragedies of his youth.\"</i><br>His youthful experiences gave the streets a lasting romantic and personal meaning.<br>Option 2 – decorations are not mentioned<br>Option 3 – political decline is not mentioned<br>Option 4 – sunsets are memories, not the cause of the streets' appearance<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Dickens’s emotional experiences gave the streets lasting personal and romantic significance.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000073880","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the following passage carefully and answer the questions that follow.<br><br>Few people truly understand the hidden life of the street. Even when we enter it, we often fail to recognise the unique individuals who belong to it—the wanderers and nomads who have preserved their secrets through generations. We understand even less about the street at night, when it resembles a great house whose doors are locked.<br>Charles Dickens, however, understood the street deeply. He seemed to possess the key to its hidden world. The street lamps were his stars, and the ordinary person on the street was his hero. He could reveal its innermost character and enter its secret passages, lined with houses and roofed with stars.<br>Facts that are merely observed do not remain permanently fixed in memory. To remember a place forever, one must experience it completely and become so deeply absorbed in it that one temporarily forgets oneself as a separate observer.<br>For Dickens, the streets remained deeply romantic because they were associated with the powerful experiences and tragedies of his youth. They were also filled with memories of sunsets that could never return. This emotional connection explains the unusual realism with which he brought the dark and ordinary corners of London to life. In his descriptions, even minor details—a window, a railing or the keyhole of a door—acquire an intense and lifelike vitality. Through his imagination, ordinary objects appear more vivid and real than they normally do.<br><br><br>Which statement best explains the unusual realism in Dickens’s descriptions? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"He exaggerated the unpleasant features of London to criticise society."},"2":{"en":"He gave ordinary physical details an intense and lifelike vitality."},"3":{"en":"He replaced realistic locations with imaginary and mysterious landscapes."},"4":{"en":"He focused only on factual accuracy and avoided emotional associations."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"In his descriptions, even minor details—a window, a railing or the keyhole of a door—acquire an intense and lifelike vitality.\"</i><br>His realism lies in making ordinary details vivid and alive.<br>Option 1 – social criticism is not mentioned<br>Option 3 – he made real places vivid, not imaginary<br>Option 4 – the passage links his realism to emotional connection<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): He gave ordinary physical details an intense and lifelike vitality.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};